1
00:00:00,534 --> 00:00:03,338
♫ In the not too distant future

2
00:00:03,338 --> 00:00:06,652
♫ Next Sunday, AD

3
00:00:06,652 --> 00:00:09,702
♫ There was a guy named Joel

4
00:00:09,702 --> 00:00:12,959
♫ Not too different from you or me

5
00:00:12,959 --> 00:00:15,715
♫ He worked at Gizmonic Institute

6
00:00:15,715 --> 00:00:19,195
♫ Just another face in a red jumpsuit

7
00:00:19,195 --> 00:00:21,918
♫ He did a good job cleaning up the place

8
00:00:21,918 --> 00:00:23,491
♫ But his bosses didn't like him

9
00:00:23,491 --> 00:00:27,324
♫ So they shot him into space

10
00:00:28,565 --> 00:00:32,732
♫ We'll send him cheesy
movies, the worst we can find

11
00:00:33,799 --> 00:00:34,733
♫ La, la, la

12
00:00:34,733 --> 00:00:37,511
♫ He'll have to sit and watch them all

13
00:00:37,511 --> 00:00:40,101
♫ Then we'll monitor his mind

14
00:00:40,101 --> 00:00:41,035
♫ La, la, la

15
00:00:41,035 --> 00:00:43,679
♫ Now keep in mind Joel can't control

16
00:00:43,679 --> 00:00:46,296
♫ Where the movies begin or end

17
00:00:46,296 --> 00:00:47,164
♫ La, la, la

18
00:00:47,164 --> 00:00:50,291
♫ Because he used those special parts

19
00:00:50,291 --> 00:00:53,958
♫ To make his robot friends

20
00:00:55,262 --> 00:00:56,697
♫ Robot roll call

21
00:00:56,697 --> 00:00:58,179
♫ Cambot, pan left

22
00:00:58,179 --> 00:00:59,674
♫ Gypsy, hi, girl

23
00:00:59,674 --> 00:01:01,362
♫ Tom Servo, what a cool guy

24
00:01:01,362 --> 00:01:02,937
♫ Crow, what a wise-cracker

25
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:05,888
♫ You're wondering how
he eats and breathes

26
00:01:05,888 --> 00:01:08,091
♫ And other science facts

27
00:01:08,091 --> 00:01:09,052
♫ La, la, la

28
00:01:09,052 --> 00:01:12,110
♫ Then repeat to yourself it's just a show

29
00:01:12,110 --> 00:01:15,247
♫ I should really just relax

30
00:01:15,247 --> 00:01:19,414
♫ For Mystery Science Theater 3000 ♫

31
00:01:29,293 --> 00:01:32,498
- [Servo] A one, a two,
we know what to do.

32
00:01:32,498 --> 00:01:34,126
♫ We're the Satellite of Love

33
00:01:34,126 --> 00:01:36,332
♫ Oh, the Satellite of Love

34
00:01:36,332 --> 00:01:40,044
♫ In spite of our
situation, we're just fine

35
00:01:40,044 --> 00:01:42,554
♫ So, forget about rejoicing

36
00:01:42,554 --> 00:01:44,610
♫ And wait for Magic Voice

37
00:01:44,610 --> 00:01:48,228
♫ It's 30 seconds to
commercial sign, we-hoo

38
00:01:48,228 --> 00:01:52,528
♫ So a couple of dumpy overlords
have shot us into space

39
00:01:52,528 --> 00:01:56,573
♫ We'll take this stupid
experiment and jam it in their face

40
00:01:56,573 --> 00:01:58,429
♫ Crow, Gypsy, Servo, Joel

41
00:01:58,429 --> 00:02:00,605
♫ Stories, fun toys

42
00:02:00,605 --> 00:02:02,541
♫ We don't care, don't despair

43
00:02:02,541 --> 00:02:04,477
♫ We're not wearin' our underwear

44
00:02:04,477 --> 00:02:08,509
♫ We're on the Satellite of Love

45
00:02:08,509 --> 00:02:10,325
♫ Warriors of the world ♫

46
00:02:10,325 --> 00:02:11,158
- By Marx!

47
00:02:11,158 --> 00:02:14,075
(upbeat pop music)

48
00:02:17,174 --> 00:02:18,883
- Alright, the best
thing about performing --

49
00:02:18,883 --> 00:02:19,716
- Yeah, right there, right there.

50
00:02:19,716 --> 00:02:20,549
Ah.

51
00:02:20,549 --> 00:02:21,727
- Is having the rockin'
wrap party afterwards.

52
00:02:21,727 --> 00:02:22,635
(cheering)

53
00:02:22,635 --> 00:02:24,440
- Yeah, alright.

54
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:25,885
- Alright, and then when
you're done with him, Tom,

55
00:02:25,885 --> 00:02:29,335
it's time for my back
rub, and then we sauna.

56
00:02:29,335 --> 00:02:30,168
(laughs)

57
00:02:30,168 --> 00:02:31,001
- Yeah, yeah, I'll give you a back rub,

58
00:02:31,001 --> 00:02:32,118
as soon as I'm done with Crow here.

59
00:02:32,118 --> 00:02:33,493
- No, I'll give you both a back rub

60
00:02:33,493 --> 00:02:35,042
when Tommy's done with me.

61
00:02:35,042 --> 00:02:35,875
- Okay.

62
00:02:35,875 --> 00:02:38,153
- I'm going to put on Bette
Midler so we can dance.

63
00:02:38,153 --> 00:02:39,488
- Yeah!
- [Crow] Aw, great idea.

64
00:02:39,488 --> 00:02:41,037
Hey, and then we can all
go down to the piano bar

65
00:02:41,037 --> 00:02:43,574
at Nuys, and sing show tunes!

66
00:02:43,574 --> 00:02:45,902
(cheering)

67
00:02:45,902 --> 00:02:48,813
- Oh, the evil impresarios
are calling, you guys.

68
00:02:48,813 --> 00:02:50,402
- Well, Weenie-Buns, I think we've

69
00:02:50,402 --> 00:02:52,271
really outdone ourselves this time.

70
00:02:52,271 --> 00:02:54,914
Not only have we found a movie
that'll make your toes curl,

71
00:02:54,914 --> 00:02:57,211
but your shoes and socks, as well.

72
00:02:57,211 --> 00:02:58,653
(laughs)

73
00:02:58,653 --> 00:03:00,976
- Yeah, I thought the
composting toilet had backed up.

74
00:03:00,976 --> 00:03:03,740
As it turns out, it's
this week's experiment.

75
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:04,608
(laughs)

76
00:03:04,608 --> 00:03:05,691
- [Both] Woo!

77
00:03:06,864 --> 00:03:07,864
- Hey, Joel?

78
00:03:11,724 --> 00:03:14,942
- But first, let's have at
that invention exchange, hmm?

79
00:03:14,942 --> 00:03:17,359
- Ah, um, I'll be right back.

80
00:03:21,391 --> 00:03:22,873
- Well, should we show 'em ours?

81
00:03:22,873 --> 00:03:25,049
- Oh, yeah, good plan.

82
00:03:25,049 --> 00:03:27,986
Hey, sirs, we have our
own invention this time.

83
00:03:27,986 --> 00:03:29,655
Cambot, move it in here --

84
00:03:29,655 --> 00:03:30,670
- Right here in my hand, Cambot.

85
00:03:30,670 --> 00:03:31,503
You see it?

86
00:03:31,503 --> 00:03:32,336
- See?

87
00:03:32,336 --> 00:03:33,800
- You see, it's a new long
distance telephone transducer,

88
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:36,003
that operates at seven ohms,
and nominal temperature

89
00:03:36,003 --> 00:03:38,112
range of zero to 50 degrees, Celsius.

90
00:03:38,112 --> 00:03:39,701
- Yeah, it's a marked improvement

91
00:03:39,701 --> 00:03:41,434
over the old configuration,
that often required

92
00:03:41,434 --> 00:03:45,074
over 25 seconds to connect
transcontinental signals.

93
00:03:45,074 --> 00:03:46,516
It does so at half the cost.

94
00:03:46,516 --> 00:03:47,349
- And it's completely solid state.

95
00:03:47,349 --> 00:03:48,425
- Mm-hmm.

96
00:03:48,425 --> 00:03:50,161
- You see, the chip
sees a telephone signal

97
00:03:50,161 --> 00:03:53,071
as a series of ones and
zeroes, which are the --

98
00:03:53,071 --> 00:03:54,420
- Hey, guys, I found out.

99
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:57,672
Here's the invention exchange,
it's called the big head.

100
00:03:57,672 --> 00:04:00,920
- Joel, we did the big head already.

101
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:01,753
- Really?

102
00:04:01,753 --> 00:04:03,470
- Yep, uh-huh.
- [Crow] Uh-huh.

103
00:04:03,470 --> 00:04:06,487
- Yes, well, let's press on, dingle-berry.

104
00:04:06,487 --> 00:04:07,320
Our --

105
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:09,144
- Hey, who's that guy with the big head?

106
00:04:09,144 --> 00:04:10,786
- Cork it, Larry.

107
00:04:10,786 --> 00:04:12,816
Our experiment this week is in honor

108
00:04:12,816 --> 00:04:15,393
of your horribly, stinky film.

109
00:04:15,393 --> 00:04:19,560
We all remember and love the
antics of comedian Joe Besser,

110
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:22,896
on the old Abbott and Costello Show.

111
00:04:22,896 --> 00:04:27,169
Well, we can relive those
moments with my new stinky bomb.

112
00:04:27,169 --> 00:04:29,415
- Yes, now you can turn
any friend into that

113
00:04:29,415 --> 00:04:32,325
lovable buffoon, who
was a lisping man-child,

114
00:04:32,325 --> 00:04:34,702
long before it became fashionable.

115
00:04:34,702 --> 00:04:38,202
- I think it would go something like this.

116
00:04:39,535 --> 00:04:40,456
(explosion)

117
00:04:40,456 --> 00:04:41,631
- Oh!

118
00:04:41,631 --> 00:04:42,539
- Elegant, isn't it?

119
00:04:42,539 --> 00:04:43,661
Yes, yes.

120
00:04:43,661 --> 00:04:44,994
- I'll harm you.

121
00:04:46,443 --> 00:04:47,765
(thud)

122
00:04:47,765 --> 00:04:48,646
(thud)

123
00:04:48,646 --> 00:04:49,568
- Well, Joel, it's time for me

124
00:04:49,568 --> 00:04:51,437
to send you your own stink bomb.

125
00:04:51,437 --> 00:04:54,575
This film makes The Unearthly
look like Citizen Kane.

126
00:04:54,575 --> 00:04:56,203
- I'll give you such a pinch, oh.

127
00:04:56,203 --> 00:04:57,036
- Ow!

128
00:04:57,036 --> 00:05:01,010
- It's called The Castle of Fu Manchu.

129
00:05:01,010 --> 00:05:01,843
(thud)

130
00:05:01,843 --> 00:05:02,676
(thud)

131
00:05:02,676 --> 00:05:04,244
- Take a tall drink of gray water, Joel.

132
00:05:04,244 --> 00:05:05,499
It'll help you get in the mood.

133
00:05:05,499 --> 00:05:06,660
Send him the film.

134
00:05:06,660 --> 00:05:07,493
- What if I don't want to.

135
00:05:07,493 --> 00:05:08,326
(cries)

136
00:05:08,326 --> 00:05:09,743
I don't want, ow!

137
00:05:10,901 --> 00:05:12,503
(thud)

138
00:05:12,503 --> 00:05:14,413
Oh, I'll harm you!

139
00:05:14,413 --> 00:05:15,371
(buzzing)

140
00:05:15,371 --> 00:05:17,454
- Movie time, movie time!

141
00:05:28,942 --> 00:05:31,078
I didn't know we had
done that one already.

142
00:05:31,078 --> 00:05:31,911
- [Crow] Yeah.

143
00:05:31,911 --> 00:05:32,744
- [Servo] Yeah, we sure,

144
00:05:32,744 --> 00:05:33,577
oh, look, it's filmed in Oakland.

145
00:05:33,577 --> 00:05:34,410
- [Crow] Hey.

146
00:05:34,410 --> 00:05:35,818
- [Joel] Oh, what a wonderful, lenten sky.

147
00:05:35,818 --> 00:05:37,553
- [Voiceover] This is Fu Manchu.

148
00:05:37,553 --> 00:05:38,386
- And you're not.

149
00:05:38,386 --> 00:05:40,878
- [Voiceover] Once again,
the world is at my mercy.

150
00:05:40,878 --> 00:05:41,839
- [Servo] Mercy!

151
00:05:41,839 --> 00:05:42,672
(growls)

152
00:05:42,672 --> 00:05:43,882
- [Voiceover] I have conquered,
not only the mysteries

153
00:05:43,882 --> 00:05:46,913
of the continent, but
now, of the oceans, too.

154
00:05:46,913 --> 00:05:48,996
- [Servo] And the ancient
secret of ventriloquism,

155
00:05:48,996 --> 00:05:50,665
now you can too!

156
00:05:50,665 --> 00:05:52,868
- [Voiceover] In the tropical
waters of the South Atlantic,

157
00:05:52,868 --> 00:05:56,513
my hand stretches out
to turn water into ice.

158
00:05:56,513 --> 00:05:58,131
- Oh, he's a refrigerator.

159
00:05:58,131 --> 00:05:59,212
- [Voiceover] And transform safety,

160
00:05:59,212 --> 00:06:01,242
into the deadliest peril.

161
00:06:01,242 --> 00:06:02,524
- [Joel] Kind of like a Corvair, huh?

162
00:06:02,524 --> 00:06:03,872
- [Voiceover] In a few moments,

163
00:06:03,872 --> 00:06:07,237
the proof of my mastery will be complete.

164
00:06:07,237 --> 00:06:09,693
- [Servo] But first, this
word from Maxwell House.

165
00:06:09,693 --> 00:06:10,601
(ragtime music)

166
00:06:10,601 --> 00:06:12,364
- [Joel] Oh, they stole
this from a Titanic movie.

167
00:06:12,364 --> 00:06:13,645
Look.

168
00:06:13,645 --> 00:06:14,478
- O, 73.

169
00:06:16,195 --> 00:06:17,971
- [Servo] We use children
to grind our hops.

170
00:06:17,971 --> 00:06:18,804
- [Man] Number three, yet?

171
00:06:18,804 --> 00:06:20,804
- [Joel] Three cherries!

172
00:06:22,740 --> 00:06:23,573
- [Servo] I wonder what this is.

173
00:06:23,573 --> 00:06:25,157
It's a Chinese personal computer.

174
00:06:25,157 --> 00:06:25,990
(laughs)

175
00:06:25,990 --> 00:06:26,823
- [Joel] Well said.

176
00:06:26,823 --> 00:06:28,588
- [Servo] Go portable.

177
00:06:28,588 --> 00:06:31,588
- They must use ninja dolphin temps.

178
00:06:32,647 --> 00:06:33,982
- There's no danger of overload.

179
00:06:33,982 --> 00:06:35,184
- [Joel] I didn't ask.

180
00:06:35,184 --> 00:06:37,467
- One of the staff in the
powerhouse make a mistake,

181
00:06:37,467 --> 00:06:39,376
generate more energy than we need.

182
00:06:39,376 --> 00:06:41,662
- I'm mixing my album, leave me alone.

183
00:06:41,662 --> 00:06:42,744
- Installed his safety lock.

184
00:06:42,744 --> 00:06:44,373
- [Servo] Oh, he's cool Fu Mo-Gee.

185
00:06:44,373 --> 00:06:45,214
(mimicking hip hop beat)

186
00:06:45,214 --> 00:06:47,217
- [Joel] Oh, he's wearing
David Byrne's big suit.

187
00:06:47,217 --> 00:06:48,050
Check it out.

188
00:06:48,050 --> 00:06:49,006
- [Servo] Oh, how about that?

189
00:06:49,006 --> 00:06:50,127
- [Crow] Big pajamas.

190
00:06:50,127 --> 00:06:52,143
- When this lever reaches
the bottom of the groove,

191
00:06:52,143 --> 00:06:53,665
we are at safety maximum.

192
00:06:53,665 --> 00:06:55,174
- [Servo] Then let your
foot off the clutch.

193
00:06:55,174 --> 00:06:58,018
- Take the lever, and move it
down into the second groove,

194
00:06:58,018 --> 00:06:59,981
before the auxiliary
channels will feed in.

195
00:06:59,981 --> 00:07:02,397
- [Servo] Auxiliary?

196
00:07:02,397 --> 00:07:03,230
(buzz)

197
00:07:03,230 --> 00:07:04,063
(gasps)
- He's flat-lining!

198
00:07:04,063 --> 00:07:07,396
- [Fu Manchu] Phase two, coming in now.

199
00:07:08,990 --> 00:07:10,740
- [Servo] Any time, come on in.

200
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:13,103
Phase two, ladies and gentlemen.

201
00:07:13,103 --> 00:07:14,945
- [Joel] Jiggle the plug,
sometimes you gotta kick it.

202
00:07:14,945 --> 00:07:18,256
(water crashing)

203
00:07:18,256 --> 00:07:19,632
- The signal isn't getting through.

204
00:07:19,632 --> 00:07:20,465
- [Servo] Hmm.

205
00:07:20,465 --> 00:07:21,298
- [Fu Manchu] Strengthen the signal.

206
00:07:21,298 --> 00:07:22,131
- No!

207
00:07:22,131 --> 00:07:22,964
- Do as I say!

208
00:07:22,964 --> 00:07:24,184
Strengthen it!

209
00:07:24,184 --> 00:07:27,095
- [Servo] Listen, my name
is on your check, buddy.

210
00:07:27,095 --> 00:07:27,928
- [Fu Manchu] More!

211
00:07:27,928 --> 00:07:29,173
- [Joel] Oh, it's a quad system.

212
00:07:29,173 --> 00:07:31,352
- We still have the safety lock.

213
00:07:31,352 --> 00:07:33,381
- Hey, don't get your
tie stuck in that thing.

214
00:07:33,381 --> 00:07:37,296
- [Joel] That's the biggest
rock tumbler I have ever seen.

215
00:07:37,296 --> 00:07:40,580
- [Servo] Big wheel, keep on turnin'.

216
00:07:40,580 --> 00:07:43,413
(mimics fog horn)

217
00:07:46,218 --> 00:07:47,953
- Do we have to see this?

218
00:07:47,953 --> 00:07:48,786
- No, we cannot!

219
00:07:48,786 --> 00:07:49,619
- Do it, do it!

220
00:07:49,619 --> 00:07:50,452
- No, no, no!

221
00:07:50,452 --> 00:07:51,285
- [Servo] Dammit, push the lever!

222
00:07:51,285 --> 00:07:52,118
- I won't do it.

223
00:07:52,118 --> 00:07:52,951
- [Servo] Will you push the lever?

224
00:07:52,951 --> 00:07:54,284
- I won't do it!

225
00:07:55,193 --> 00:07:56,488
- [Servo] It's Witness, all of a sudden.

226
00:07:56,488 --> 00:07:57,449
(laughs)

227
00:07:57,449 --> 00:08:00,936
- Lin Tang, slide that lever over.

228
00:08:00,936 --> 00:08:02,178
Slide it over and hold it!

229
00:08:02,178 --> 00:08:03,761
- [Joel] That girl!

230
00:08:07,829 --> 00:08:08,662
- [Servo] Like this?

231
00:08:08,662 --> 00:08:10,352
- Oh, yes, oh, yes.

232
00:08:10,352 --> 00:08:11,300
Girth.

233
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:14,133
(mimics fog horn)

234
00:08:20,419 --> 00:08:21,252
(gun shot)

235
00:08:21,252 --> 00:08:22,238
- [Servo] Oh, she exploded.

236
00:08:22,238 --> 00:08:23,426
Oh.
- [Crow] Oh.

237
00:08:23,426 --> 00:08:25,295
- [Servo] Thought she'd --

238
00:08:25,295 --> 00:08:26,350
(suspenseful music)

239
00:08:26,350 --> 00:08:27,992
- [Joel] Looks like my freezer.

240
00:08:27,992 --> 00:08:28,825
(yells)

241
00:08:28,825 --> 00:08:32,411
- [Servo] Ooh, gotta do
something about that.

242
00:08:32,411 --> 00:08:34,307
- [Joel] Deploy the
bread, deploy the bread.

243
00:08:34,307 --> 00:08:35,390
Wonder bread.

244
00:08:36,577 --> 00:08:37,912
- Lucy must be around here somewhere.

245
00:08:37,912 --> 00:08:38,745
(laughs)

246
00:08:38,745 --> 00:08:40,289
Ah, Ricky, I hit an iceberg.

247
00:08:40,289 --> 00:08:41,122
Ah.

248
00:08:42,118 --> 00:08:42,951
- [Joel] Call it quits.

249
00:08:42,951 --> 00:08:44,601
That pretty much screws
up the shuffleboard.

250
00:08:44,601 --> 00:08:46,099
Come on.

251
00:08:46,099 --> 00:08:48,796
- [Servo] Hey, the water
got warmer in here.

252
00:08:48,796 --> 00:08:51,387
- Thank you, Wang, that'll be all.

253
00:08:51,387 --> 00:08:55,165
- [Joel] Nose to the grindstone, you.

254
00:08:55,165 --> 00:08:56,207
- [Servo] Oh, somebody wet the bed.

255
00:08:56,207 --> 00:08:57,040
(laughs)

256
00:08:57,040 --> 00:08:58,076
- So, I called down the desk clerk.

257
00:08:58,076 --> 00:08:59,358
I said, "I had a leak in the sink".

258
00:08:59,358 --> 00:09:01,040
He said, "Go ahead, the
customer's always right."

259
