518
00:17:52,710 --> 00:17:55,861
- [Joel] Rula Lenska as the
Turkish lieutenant's woman.

519
00:17:55,861 --> 00:17:57,477
(laughs)

520
00:17:57,477 --> 00:17:58,758
- Gee, I don't recognize him,

521
00:17:58,758 --> 00:18:00,093
but the fez is familiar.

522
00:18:00,093 --> 00:18:02,110
(mimics rim shot)

523
00:18:02,110 --> 00:18:05,741
- [Servo] Either I'm weird,
or that guy's really hot.

524
00:18:05,741 --> 00:18:08,134
- Oh, it's Annie Hall.

525
00:18:08,134 --> 00:18:09,669
- [Joel] Bet he's smokin' a Camel, huh?

526
00:18:09,669 --> 00:18:10,911
(laughs)

527
00:18:10,911 --> 00:18:13,994
- [Servo] Turkish and domestic blend.

528
00:18:16,572 --> 00:18:19,655
(ominous jazz music)

529
00:18:20,898 --> 00:18:24,129
- It's like a meeting
of the Shriner Mafia.

530
00:18:24,129 --> 00:18:25,825
- [Servo] Do you like this pole?

531
00:18:25,825 --> 00:18:27,801
- This water splits out.

532
00:18:27,801 --> 00:18:28,634
- [Crow] What?

533
00:18:28,634 --> 00:18:30,634
- The search of the sun.

534
00:18:32,009 --> 00:18:33,867
- I have been sent by Omar Pasha --

535
00:18:33,867 --> 00:18:36,349
- [Joel] There goes a spooky sub.

536
00:18:36,349 --> 00:18:39,099
- Good, we have no time to waste.

537
00:18:40,421 --> 00:18:41,838
- Yeah, whatever.

538
00:18:42,998 --> 00:18:44,493
- [Servo] Hey, look,
Pac-Man's got his own flag.

539
00:18:44,493 --> 00:18:45,493
- [Joel] Oh.

540
00:18:48,525 --> 00:18:51,970
- We're just two ships
passing in the, uh, day.

541
00:18:51,970 --> 00:18:53,172
(laughs)

542
00:18:53,172 --> 00:18:55,468
(humming)

543
00:18:55,468 --> 00:18:58,051
- [Joel] Catalina Caper, right?

544
00:19:00,715 --> 00:19:01,548
Are you following me?

545
00:19:01,548 --> 00:19:02,918
Quit following me.

546
00:19:02,918 --> 00:19:05,585
(ominous music)

547
00:19:09,674 --> 00:19:11,984
Heel, I don't want you following me.

548
00:19:11,984 --> 00:19:15,121
- All we are is dust in the wind, man.

549
00:19:15,121 --> 00:19:17,121
- [Joel] That's so true.

550
00:19:20,222 --> 00:19:24,389
♫ I have often walked
down this road before ♫

551
00:19:27,805 --> 00:19:28,638
- [Servo] Well, you see.

552
00:19:28,638 --> 00:19:29,471
The theory is you're harder to see,

553
00:19:29,471 --> 00:19:31,851
when you sneak around like that.

554
00:19:31,851 --> 00:19:32,684
(bubbling)

555
00:19:32,684 --> 00:19:35,282
- Next, we travel to
Istanbul with Robert Goulet,

556
00:19:35,282 --> 00:19:39,154
as he hooks up with that non-co-sheggie.

557
00:19:39,154 --> 00:19:40,209
- [Joel] Janie?

558
00:19:40,209 --> 00:19:42,412
- Master, I have brought the lady.

559
00:19:42,412 --> 00:19:44,329
- Oh, wow, I'm so high.

560
00:19:45,456 --> 00:19:47,192
- [Servo] Excuse me, while I kiss the sky.

561
00:19:47,192 --> 00:19:48,692
- Persistent lady.

562
00:19:51,905 --> 00:19:53,120
Greetings.

563
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:54,629
Sit down please.

564
00:19:54,629 --> 00:19:56,962
- [Servo] I am sitting down.

565
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:04,789
- You have received my message?

566
00:20:04,789 --> 00:20:07,486
- What have you to sell me?

567
00:20:07,486 --> 00:20:09,035
- Opium.

568
00:20:09,035 --> 00:20:09,876
- [Servo] Hmm.

569
00:20:09,876 --> 00:20:11,785
- I have enough opium.

570
00:20:11,785 --> 00:20:13,080
- [Crow] How about Chanel No 5?

571
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:17,393
- To control the trade
of half of the world.

572
00:20:17,393 --> 00:20:21,011
- You are starting to interest me.

573
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:23,388
- You are one of the few that
passed the governor's castle.

574
00:20:23,388 --> 00:20:26,315
- [Servo] The proud, the Marines.

575
00:20:26,315 --> 00:20:27,530
- Yes?

576
00:20:27,530 --> 00:20:30,605
- The governor's castle
contains the biggest reserve

577
00:20:30,605 --> 00:20:32,937
of opium in the East, but the --

578
00:20:32,937 --> 00:20:34,018
- [Joel] What are we waiting for then?

579
00:20:34,018 --> 00:20:35,567
Road trip, dude.

580
00:20:35,567 --> 00:20:36,555
Whoa.
- [Crow] Woo!

581
00:20:36,555 --> 00:20:37,463
- I'm interested.

582
00:20:37,463 --> 00:20:40,120
- If you agree, we will share the opium.

583
00:20:40,120 --> 00:20:41,148
- [Crow] With her and her roommates.

584
00:20:41,148 --> 00:20:42,416
- Explain to me your plans.

585
00:20:42,416 --> 00:20:43,458
- [Voiceover] You will send your men

586
00:20:43,458 --> 00:20:45,701
up the river Bosphorus --

587
00:20:45,701 --> 00:20:46,534
- [Servo] We gotta go, guys.

588
00:20:46,534 --> 00:20:48,284
Oh, this movie's bad.

589
00:20:51,207 --> 00:20:52,743
- [Voiceover] Leaving the way clear,

590
00:20:52,743 --> 00:20:55,993
for me and my men, to approach on feet.

591
00:21:04,759 --> 00:21:06,759
(cries)

592
00:21:09,953 --> 00:21:11,822
- Oh, are we on?

593
00:21:11,822 --> 00:21:13,518
(clears throat)

594
00:21:13,518 --> 00:21:18,404
The Miss Saigon Syndrome, an
editorial by Crow T. Robot.

595
00:21:18,404 --> 00:21:20,527
Dear Miss, Sir, or Madame,

596
00:21:20,527 --> 00:21:24,427
I can no longer sit idly by
on my little robot haunches,

597
00:21:24,427 --> 00:21:25,975
and watch Caucasian actors being

598
00:21:25,975 --> 00:21:28,925
continually cast in non-Caucasian roles.

599
00:21:28,925 --> 00:21:31,809
Christoper Lee's portrayal
of Fu Manchu is a crystalline

600
00:21:31,809 --> 00:21:34,266
example of the phenomenon I have tried,

601
00:21:34,266 --> 00:21:36,723
titled, Bad Actors, Bad Decisions.

602
00:21:36,723 --> 00:21:37,556
(sniffs)

603
00:21:37,556 --> 00:21:38,389
Sorry.

604
00:21:38,389 --> 00:21:39,788
This insidious tradition
of casting, has formed

605
00:21:39,788 --> 00:21:42,045
a psychological backdrop,
in which we play out

606
00:21:42,045 --> 00:21:45,423
the insignificant comings and
goings of our daily lives.

607
00:21:45,423 --> 00:21:49,481
Let me, Crow T. Robot, pull
back the curtain, to reveal

608
00:21:49,481 --> 00:21:52,005
the lie, on which your life is based.

609
00:21:52,005 --> 00:21:54,462
Sign post number one on
your road to discovery,

610
00:21:54,462 --> 00:21:57,813
George Pal's enchanting,
The Seven Faces of Dr. Lao.

611
00:21:57,813 --> 00:21:59,928
Would it shock you to know that
all seven faces were played

612
00:21:59,928 --> 00:22:03,468
by the white, musical
theater actor, Tony Randall?

613
00:22:03,468 --> 00:22:04,301
Wake up, people!

614
00:22:04,301 --> 00:22:05,896
That's seven examples right there.

615
00:22:05,896 --> 00:22:07,338
Now you're saying to yourself,

616
00:22:07,338 --> 00:22:09,782
"Please, Mr. Robot, carrier of
the gleaming sword of truth,

617
00:22:09,782 --> 00:22:11,330
"don't spoil the shining obelisk

618
00:22:11,330 --> 00:22:14,388
"of Sunday afternoon
enjoyment, Charlie Chan."

619
00:22:14,388 --> 00:22:15,897
Sorry, it's my job.

620
00:22:15,897 --> 00:22:18,674
Charlie Chan is a Swede,
named Warner Oland.

621
00:22:18,674 --> 00:22:19,675
"Crow, stop now!

622
00:22:19,675 --> 00:22:20,641
"You're woozy!"

623
00:22:20,641 --> 00:22:22,586
No, the truth is a runaway train.

624
00:22:22,586 --> 00:22:23,867
Who's that playing an Asian in

625
00:22:23,867 --> 00:22:25,741
The Tea House of The August Moon?

626
00:22:25,741 --> 00:22:28,287
It's your precious method
actor, Marlon Brando.

627
00:22:28,287 --> 00:22:29,168
Here's a bonus.

628
00:22:29,168 --> 00:22:30,322
The Indian Chief on F Troop

629
00:22:30,322 --> 00:22:32,805
was a grade-D actor, Frank Nakoa.

630
00:22:32,805 --> 00:22:34,349
Dare I go on?

631
00:22:34,349 --> 00:22:35,182
(crying)

632
00:22:35,182 --> 00:22:36,715
What's the point?

633
00:22:36,715 --> 00:22:38,317
- Crow, buddy, control yourself.

634
00:22:38,317 --> 00:22:39,559
You're getting off track.

635
00:22:39,559 --> 00:22:41,842
The kids out there love
your acerbic editorials.

636
00:22:41,842 --> 00:22:42,763
Stick it to the man!

637
00:22:42,763 --> 00:22:44,567
You can't let them down.

638
00:22:44,567 --> 00:22:46,200
- But it hurts too much.

639
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:47,033
- Buck up, Crow.

640
00:22:47,033 --> 00:22:48,736
Get out there and do it for the kids!

641
00:22:48,736 --> 00:22:49,569
Come on!

642
00:22:49,569 --> 00:22:51,652
(crying)

643
00:22:52,515 --> 00:22:53,348
- Okay.

644
00:22:54,787 --> 00:22:56,456
Anyway, where was I?

645
00:22:56,456 --> 00:23:00,048
So, in conclusion, Cameron
Mackintosh, bite me!

646
00:23:00,048 --> 00:23:00,881
Oh, wait.

647
00:23:00,881 --> 00:23:02,758
There are so many examples I should give.

648
00:23:02,758 --> 00:23:05,282
What about Joey Bishop in Sergeants 3?

649
00:23:05,282 --> 00:23:07,685
Hey, wait a minute, I like
Joey Bishop in that movie.

650
00:23:07,685 --> 00:23:09,643
He's in a category by himself.

651
00:23:09,643 --> 00:23:11,846
He's always good, no
matter what role he plays.

652
00:23:11,846 --> 00:23:13,555
Regis Philbin had no right to walk

653
00:23:13,555 --> 00:23:14,903
off his show the way he did.

654
00:23:14,903 --> 00:23:15,736
How could he do that?

655
00:23:15,736 --> 00:23:16,569
Why?

656
00:23:16,569 --> 00:23:17,402
Why?

657
00:23:17,402 --> 00:23:18,235
Why?

658
00:23:18,235 --> 00:23:19,068
(crying)

659
00:23:19,068 --> 00:23:19,901
- No.

660
00:23:19,901 --> 00:23:21,168
(crying)

661
00:23:21,168 --> 00:23:22,335
Joel, help us.

662
00:23:23,785 --> 00:23:25,494
- Look at what you've
done to my little friends.

663
00:23:25,494 --> 00:23:26,855
Are you guys happy now?

664
00:23:26,855 --> 00:23:28,017
Come on, it's okay, buddy.

665
00:23:28,017 --> 00:23:28,850
- Don't you care?

666
00:23:28,850 --> 00:23:31,275
Don't you even care?

667
00:23:31,275 --> 00:23:34,786
- Our data is showing deep,
deep pain, all around.

668
00:23:34,786 --> 00:23:36,001
Well, it looks like we could expect

669
00:23:36,001 --> 00:23:38,939
to get a Nobel Prize for evil, Frank.

670
00:23:38,939 --> 00:23:41,189
(laughing)

671
00:23:51,716 --> 00:23:53,785
(gasping)

672
00:23:53,785 --> 00:23:56,296
- Better send 'em a commercial.

673
00:23:56,296 --> 00:23:59,213
(upbeat pop music)

674
00:24:03,065 --> 00:24:04,146
- [Joel] Oh, it's not that bad.

675
00:24:04,146 --> 00:24:06,379
- [Servo] It's pretty bad.

676
00:24:06,379 --> 00:24:07,212
- [Joel] Not more.

677
00:24:07,212 --> 00:24:09,045
- [Servo] Tell a joke.

678
00:24:10,251 --> 00:24:11,399
- Oh, Laurel and Hardy are there.

679
00:24:11,399 --> 00:24:12,232
(laughs)

680
00:24:12,232 --> 00:24:13,097
- [Servo] That's a good one.

681
00:24:13,097 --> 00:24:14,833
- I have a pass to see the governor.

682
00:24:14,833 --> 00:24:17,450
- [Joel] I was in Victor Victoria.

683
00:24:17,450 --> 00:24:18,291
- [Servo] Here, let me see that.

684
00:24:18,291 --> 00:24:20,107
"Please excuse Carol from," what is this?

685
00:24:20,107 --> 00:24:21,940
- [Man] Open the gate!

686
00:24:26,626 --> 00:24:29,333
(clears throat)

687
00:24:29,333 --> 00:24:30,948
- [Joel] Now close it, real fast.

688
00:24:30,948 --> 00:24:33,031
(laughs)

689
00:24:35,421 --> 00:24:37,036
- That girl!

690
00:24:37,036 --> 00:24:38,203
- [Servo] Hmm.

691
00:24:42,778 --> 00:24:44,727
(gun shots)

692
00:24:44,727 --> 00:24:45,560
- [Servo] Oh, no!

693
00:24:45,560 --> 00:24:46,877
Bob Hope is killing people!

694
00:24:46,877 --> 00:24:49,294
- Take that you fez monsters.

695
00:24:51,643 --> 00:24:52,476
(gun shot)

696
00:24:52,476 --> 00:24:53,309
- [Joel] Pull!

697
00:24:53,309 --> 00:24:55,291
(laughs)

698
00:24:55,291 --> 00:24:57,080
- [Servo] Oh, it's got flare.

699
00:24:57,080 --> 00:24:59,497
- I guess that means come on.

700
00:25:01,152 --> 00:25:04,319
- [Servo] Oh, Mrs. Peel, we're needed.

701
00:25:08,736 --> 00:25:12,653
- [Joel] Two stairs
diverge into a yellow wood.

702
00:25:14,223 --> 00:25:15,398
- [Servo] Looks like Graceland.

703
00:25:15,398 --> 00:25:18,576
Graceland, Memphis, Tennessee.

704
00:25:18,576 --> 00:25:19,537
- I see Elvis.

705
00:25:19,537 --> 00:25:20,370
(gasps)

706
00:25:20,370 --> 00:25:21,203
- [Servo] Where?

707
00:25:21,203 --> 00:25:22,354
Where?

708
00:25:22,354 --> 00:25:23,465
- Carry me, carry me!

709
00:25:23,465 --> 00:25:24,298
Hey, pile on Uncle Bob.

710
00:25:24,298 --> 00:25:26,881
Tickle machine, tickle machine.

711
00:25:28,728 --> 00:25:29,561
- [Joel] Does this bug you?

712
00:25:29,561 --> 00:25:30,424
I'm not touching you.

713
00:25:30,424 --> 00:25:31,826
Does this bug you?

714
00:25:31,826 --> 00:25:34,409
- [Servo] Oh, bloodless guards.

715
00:25:35,743 --> 00:25:36,691
- [Crow] Thorazine guards.

716
00:25:36,691 --> 00:25:38,574
(laughs)

717
00:25:38,574 --> 00:25:40,657
(humming)

718
00:25:40,657 --> 00:25:42,008
(yells)

719
00:25:42,008 --> 00:25:43,258
- [Servo] Yawn.

720
00:25:45,533 --> 00:25:46,366
(screams)

721
00:25:46,366 --> 00:25:47,536
- [Joel] It's the killer joke.

722
00:25:47,536 --> 00:25:49,098
(laughs)

723
00:25:49,098 --> 00:25:50,299
Sure glad I dressed to move.

724
00:25:50,299 --> 00:25:51,132
You?

725
00:25:51,132 --> 00:25:52,132
- [Crow] Mm.

726
00:25:53,597 --> 00:25:54,430
(gunshots)

727
00:25:54,430 --> 00:25:55,347
Jawbreaker?

728
00:25:56,735 --> 00:25:58,985
(gunshots)

729
00:26:02,142 --> 00:26:03,384
- [Servo] Chester A. Arthur?

730
00:26:03,384 --> 00:26:06,084
Ooh, the press shot us a buffalo there.

731
00:26:06,084 --> 00:26:07,334
- [Joel] Mommy?

732
00:26:08,949 --> 00:26:11,032
- Boy, could you tell me what day it is?

733
00:26:11,032 --> 00:26:12,901
- [Joel] Why, it's Christmas Day, sir.

734
00:26:12,901 --> 00:26:14,223
- Mutt?

735
00:26:14,223 --> 00:26:15,064
Mutt?

736
00:26:15,064 --> 00:26:18,041
(dog barking)

737
00:26:18,041 --> 00:26:19,176
- [Joel] Grover Cleveland?

738
00:26:19,176 --> 00:26:21,509
- [Servo] Oh, there you are.

739
00:26:22,773 --> 00:26:23,606
(laughs)

740
00:26:23,606 --> 00:26:26,495
- Hey, who hasn't had
a nightmare like this?

741
00:26:26,495 --> 00:26:28,742
- [Servo] My lord.

742
00:26:28,742 --> 00:26:31,145
Oh, oh, it's you guys again.

743
00:26:31,145 --> 00:26:31,978
Hello.

744
00:26:34,296 --> 00:26:35,297
(whimpering)

745
00:26:35,297 --> 00:26:37,297
- Oh, swords, smimatars.

746
00:26:38,168 --> 00:26:39,049
Hmm.

747
00:26:39,049 --> 00:26:39,916
(laughs)

748
00:26:39,916 --> 00:26:41,833
- [Man Running] Guards!

749
00:26:44,197 --> 00:26:46,376
- [Servo] Alright,
everybody, it's a B Major.

750
00:26:46,376 --> 00:26:50,315
- [Joel] He's being
attacked by a swing choir.

751
00:26:50,315 --> 00:26:51,597
- Kareem!

752
00:26:51,597 --> 00:26:53,253
- [Joel] Oh, he's standing
on an office chair.

753
00:26:53,253 --> 00:26:54,086
- Oh.

754
00:26:55,295 --> 00:26:56,128
- Lin Tang?

755
00:26:56,128 --> 00:26:56,961
- Yes, father.

756
00:26:56,961 --> 00:26:57,928
- [Servo] Hello, we
are your new neighbors.

757
00:26:57,928 --> 00:27:00,011
May we borrow some pesto?

758
00:27:04,954 --> 00:27:06,623
(gasps)

759
00:27:06,623 --> 00:27:08,439
- [Fu Manchu] Proceed, daughter.

760
00:27:08,439 --> 00:27:09,689
- [Servo] Okay.

761
00:27:10,602 --> 00:27:13,472
- [Joel] If you don't look
good, we don't look good.

762
00:27:13,472 --> 00:27:14,305
Oops.

763
00:27:14,305 --> 00:27:16,388
(laughs)

764
00:27:17,451 --> 00:27:18,951
- Sorry, I missed.

765
00:27:21,697 --> 00:27:24,300
- [Joel] And now the cast of My Fair Lady.

766
00:27:24,300 --> 00:27:26,217
- You have fought well.

767
00:27:27,865 --> 00:27:31,323
We are grateful to you, for
opening the doors to us.

768
00:27:31,323 --> 00:27:32,485
- It was nothing.

769
00:27:32,485 --> 00:27:33,318
- [Servo] Nothing.

770
00:27:33,318 --> 00:27:35,996
- We were able to approach unseen.

771
00:27:35,996 --> 00:27:38,720
- We are very happy to serve you.

772
00:27:38,720 --> 00:27:39,970
- Check please!

773
00:27:41,113 --> 00:27:42,982
- [Servo] Uh-oh.

774
00:27:42,982 --> 00:27:44,517
- [Joel] A rat-ta-tat-tat.

775
00:27:44,517 --> 00:27:45,767
Rat-ta-tat-tat.

776
00:27:47,001 --> 00:27:47,834
(gunshots)

777
00:27:47,834 --> 00:27:50,751
- [Servo] Bob Hope is The Mechanic.

778
00:27:56,243 --> 00:27:58,726
- Isn't she helpful?

779
00:27:58,726 --> 00:28:00,393
- [Joel] Over there.

780
00:28:01,837 --> 00:28:04,748
(grunts)

781
00:28:04,748 --> 00:28:06,216
He's strict, that one.

782
00:28:06,216 --> 00:28:07,373
