00:37:38,020 --> 00:37:40,172
- [Joel] So I don't like him anymore.

1041
00:37:40,172 --> 00:37:41,294
- Do you know where he is now?

1042
00:37:41,294 --> 00:37:43,210
- Well, here's a stab, Joe's Bar?

1043
00:37:43,210 --> 00:37:44,688
- He called me last week,

1044
00:37:44,688 --> 00:37:46,424
to tell me he's going to the continent.

1045
00:37:46,424 --> 00:37:47,257
- [Servo] No, no, you fool!

1046
00:37:47,257 --> 00:37:48,674
He's incontinent.

1047
00:37:49,604 --> 00:37:52,515
- Some days ago I had a card from Athens.

1048
00:37:52,515 --> 00:37:54,264
- [Joel] She turned into a mannequin.

1049
00:37:54,264 --> 00:37:55,839
- [Kessler] Look, I've
go it here, somewhere.

1050
00:37:55,839 --> 00:37:57,375
If I can just find it.

1051
00:37:57,375 --> 00:37:58,208
- [Crow] Hmm, not bad.

1052
00:37:58,208 --> 00:37:59,291
Later, later.

1053
00:38:03,329 --> 00:38:04,625
- [Servo] Oh, no, that's disgusting.

1054
00:38:04,625 --> 00:38:06,723
A picture of you and Oliver Reed.

1055
00:38:06,723 --> 00:38:09,065
- What the devil is he
doing so far from England?

1056
00:38:09,065 --> 00:38:12,251
- He mentions on the card that
he's moving on to Istanbul.

1057
00:38:12,251 --> 00:38:13,119
- Istanbul?

1058
00:38:13,119 --> 00:38:14,708
What's he doing, the circular trip?

1059
00:38:14,708 --> 00:38:16,270
(knocks on door)

1060
00:38:16,270 --> 00:38:17,271
- Ingrid --

1061
00:38:17,271 --> 00:38:19,194
- [Crow] Get some more actors
in this scene, will you?

1062
00:38:19,194 --> 00:38:20,302
- Would you please tell
them that I'm busy?

1063
00:38:20,302 --> 00:38:21,135
- Yes, yes, don't worry.

1064
00:38:21,135 --> 00:38:21,968
I'll send them away.

1065
00:38:21,968 --> 00:38:23,066
- [Crow] Hey, let's not
clue the audience in

1066
00:38:23,066 --> 00:38:25,672
on the plot yet, okay?

1067
00:38:25,672 --> 00:38:28,172
- [Joel] Let's ditch her, huh?

1068
00:38:36,033 --> 00:38:37,448
- [Servo] Would you like
one of our watchtowers?

1069
00:38:37,448 --> 00:38:38,903
(percussive music)

1070
00:38:38,903 --> 00:38:39,736
- Does this bug you?

1071
00:38:39,736 --> 00:38:40,569
Does this bug you?

1072
00:38:40,569 --> 00:38:42,295
I'm not touching you.

1073
00:38:42,295 --> 00:38:44,878
- [Joel] Doggone, take me away.

1074
00:38:45,753 --> 00:38:47,609
- I know nothing about
Heracles' experiments --

1075
00:38:47,609 --> 00:38:48,442
- [Servo] Nothing!

1076
00:38:48,442 --> 00:38:49,275
Nothing!

1077
00:38:52,442 --> 00:38:56,901
- He would want to benefit
mankind, not to destroy it.

1078
00:38:56,901 --> 00:39:00,549
- Fu Manchu is only
interested in destruction.

1079
00:39:00,549 --> 00:39:02,381
- [Crow] Hey, he's making
a Xerox copy of his butt.

1080
00:39:02,381 --> 00:39:04,036
- [Servo] Hey, what do you know?

1081
00:39:04,036 --> 00:39:04,869
- I believe it's a question

1082
00:39:04,869 --> 00:39:06,974
of saving the world, Dr. Kessler.

1083
00:39:06,974 --> 00:39:08,705
- [Servo] Oh, that.

1084
00:39:08,705 --> 00:39:11,583
- [Joel] Leave the
specimens alone, please.

1085
00:39:11,583 --> 00:39:14,240
- [Servo] I think it would
be fun to go to Istanbul.

1086
00:39:14,240 --> 00:39:15,401
- [Joel] Oh, that would be fun.

1087
00:39:15,401 --> 00:39:16,234
- Well then, if I may, I will come

1088
00:39:16,234 --> 00:39:18,074
with you, and maybe Ingrid, too.

1089
00:39:18,074 --> 00:39:19,089
- Good.

1090
00:39:19,089 --> 00:39:20,304
- Thank you.

1091
00:39:20,304 --> 00:39:24,471
- [Joel] We'll make it a
holiday, a camping holiday.

1092
00:39:25,698 --> 00:39:27,436
- [Crow] Damn, this
tobacco is really good.

1093
00:39:27,436 --> 00:39:30,186
(knocks on door)

1094
00:39:31,682 --> 00:39:35,194
- [Joel] Only you can prevent desk fires.

1095
00:39:35,194 --> 00:39:37,480
- [Servo] Land shark.

1096
00:39:37,480 --> 00:39:38,563
- Tickle-Ray.

1097
00:39:39,549 --> 00:39:41,799
- [Joel] Miss Jane Pittman.

1098
00:39:46,679 --> 00:39:49,582
- [Servo] Time for go to bed.

1099
00:39:49,582 --> 00:39:53,066
- [Sir Dennis] I wonder
what's keeping Kessler?

1100
00:39:53,066 --> 00:39:57,233
- Gee, this is the most
action we've seen, so far.

1101
00:39:59,715 --> 00:40:01,665
- [Joel] Smells like
a dead monkey in here.

1102
00:40:01,665 --> 00:40:02,498
You?

1103
00:40:04,215 --> 00:40:05,750
- [Servo] It's not funny anymore, guys.

1104
00:40:05,750 --> 00:40:06,805
I can't take this anymore.

1105
00:40:06,805 --> 00:40:07,638
I'm getting out of here.

1106
00:40:07,638 --> 00:40:08,661
Get me out of here please.

1107
00:40:08,661 --> 00:40:09,494
- [Joel] Oh, geez, come on.

1108
00:40:09,494 --> 00:40:10,327
Okay, jeepers.

1109
00:40:10,327 --> 00:40:11,331
- [Servo] This film is too terrible.

1110
00:40:11,331 --> 00:40:12,386
- Kessler didn't mean to
leave a cigarette burn,

1111
00:40:12,386 --> 00:40:13,908
into a polished wood table.

1112
00:40:13,908 --> 00:40:16,825
(upbeat pop music)

1113
00:40:19,836 --> 00:40:22,733
- Ah, come in, Red Shriner
Sergeant-At-Arms Joel.

1114
00:40:22,733 --> 00:40:24,522
This is Black Shriner Leader, Tom.

1115
00:40:24,522 --> 00:40:26,044
Come in boys, and cut the comedy.

1116
00:40:26,044 --> 00:40:26,877
I'm in trouble here.

1117
00:40:26,877 --> 00:40:27,740
Over.

1118
00:40:27,740 --> 00:40:29,115
- [Joel] Ah, yeah, Shriner Leader Tom,

1119
00:40:29,115 --> 00:40:31,719
this is Red Shriner
Joel, at your backdoor,

1120
00:40:31,719 --> 00:40:33,655
with Neon Peon Crow in tow.

1121
00:40:33,655 --> 00:40:34,603
What's your 20?

1122
00:40:34,603 --> 00:40:35,524
- What's my 20?

1123
00:40:35,524 --> 00:40:36,632
Sweet Sons of Norway, man!

1124
00:40:36,632 --> 00:40:37,981
My magic carpet's malfunctioned,

1125
00:40:37,981 --> 00:40:39,730
and I'm stuck in front
of the Robert Hall store,

1126
00:40:39,730 --> 00:40:40,611
on the Main Street.

1127
00:40:40,611 --> 00:40:42,560
On top of that, I've run
out of Jolly Rancher candy,

1128
00:40:42,560 --> 00:40:44,122
and the kids are startin' to look ugly.

1129
00:40:44,122 --> 00:40:44,955
Over.

1130
00:40:44,955 --> 00:40:46,148
- [Crow] Ace to ya, good buddy.

1131
00:40:46,148 --> 00:40:47,807
This is the Neon Peon.

1132
00:40:47,807 --> 00:40:49,214
I'm in your rockin' chair.

1133
00:40:49,214 --> 00:40:51,599
Hold tight, Shriner Leader Joel and I,

1134
00:40:51,599 --> 00:40:52,814
about to do a flyover.

1135
00:40:52,814 --> 00:40:53,647
- Hurry up, man.

1136
00:40:53,647 --> 00:40:54,777
I'm running out of hard candy.

1137
00:40:54,777 --> 00:40:55,610
Condition red.

1138
00:40:55,610 --> 00:40:56,708
Send in the clowns.

1139
00:40:56,708 --> 00:40:57,549
What's the use?

1140
00:40:57,549 --> 00:40:59,632
(crying)

1141
00:41:00,836 --> 00:41:01,904
- Aw, man, Joel.

1142
00:41:01,904 --> 00:41:03,493
He's totally off script.

1143
00:41:03,493 --> 00:41:04,486
There's nothing that says anything

1144
00:41:04,486 --> 00:41:06,430
about sounding like a broken man.

1145
00:41:06,430 --> 00:41:07,472
- Yeah, you're right.

1146
00:41:07,472 --> 00:41:09,725
Let's see, it says here, Tom says,

1147
00:41:09,725 --> 00:41:12,618
"Tighten formation, men,
those kids are all over me.

1148
00:41:12,618 --> 00:41:14,129
"Argh."

1149
00:41:14,129 --> 00:41:15,384
It just says, "Argh," it doesn't say

1150
00:41:15,384 --> 00:41:17,667
anything about sobbing pitifully.

1151
00:41:17,667 --> 00:41:18,508
- I can't do it, guys.

1152
00:41:18,508 --> 00:41:19,470
I just can't do it.

1153
00:41:19,470 --> 00:41:20,765
I can't go through another
sketch, loosely based

1154
00:41:20,765 --> 00:41:23,355
on some vague reference of the movie.

1155
00:41:23,355 --> 00:41:25,131
There are only a few kinds
of fezzes in this movie,

1156
00:41:25,131 --> 00:41:27,657
and suddenly, we're the
Sahara Shriners, riding flying

1157
00:41:27,657 --> 00:41:29,032
carpets on Maxwell Street Days.

1158
00:41:29,032 --> 00:41:29,865
Why?

1159
00:41:31,436 --> 00:41:32,477
Get me out of here.

1160
00:41:32,477 --> 00:41:33,310
- I don't understand.

1161
00:41:33,310 --> 00:41:34,226
How is this sketch any different

1162
00:41:34,226 --> 00:41:36,175
than anything else we do, during a movie?

1163
00:41:36,175 --> 00:41:39,033
- Well, Crow, it's not the
sketch, it's this movie.

1164
00:41:39,033 --> 00:41:39,866
Look at him.

1165
00:41:39,866 --> 00:41:41,035
He's just a broken man.

1166
00:41:41,035 --> 00:41:41,868
- You're tellin' me.

1167
00:41:41,868 --> 00:41:42,798
There are absolutely no psychological

1168
00:41:42,798 --> 00:41:43,919
footholds in this film.

1169
00:41:43,919 --> 00:41:45,802
It's like trying to climb El Capitan.

1170
00:41:45,802 --> 00:41:46,977
There's something wrong with me!

1171
00:41:46,977 --> 00:41:47,978
There's something wrong with me!

1172
00:41:47,978 --> 00:41:48,811
Why!

1173
00:41:48,811 --> 00:41:49,644
Why!

1174
00:41:49,644 --> 00:41:50,477
(sobbing)

1175
00:41:50,477 --> 00:41:51,310
- Better you than me.

1176
00:41:51,310 --> 00:41:52,143
- Oh, Crow, come on.

1177
00:41:52,143 --> 00:41:52,976
Look at what you've done to him.

1178
00:41:52,976 --> 00:41:53,853
- Me?

1179
00:41:53,853 --> 00:41:55,992
- Do you see what you've done to this guy?

1180
00:41:55,992 --> 00:41:57,233
Come on!

1181
00:41:57,233 --> 00:41:58,715
- You see, Frank, it feels good

1182
00:41:58,715 --> 00:42:00,264
to be with the winners, doesn't it?

1183
00:42:00,264 --> 00:42:01,225
- Oh, yes.

1184
00:42:01,225 --> 00:42:02,667
- Hey, let's order out.

1185
00:42:02,667 --> 00:42:03,818
Mongolian?

1186
00:42:03,818 --> 00:42:05,558
- I was thinking more
along the lines of one

1187
00:42:05,558 --> 00:42:09,525
of those delightful, stuffed
pesto pizzas from Eduardo's.

1188
00:42:09,525 --> 00:42:11,888
- Hmm, you fly, I'll buy.

1189
00:42:11,888 --> 00:42:13,344
- Solid, Jackson.

1190
00:42:13,344 --> 00:42:15,159
(laughs)

1191
00:42:15,159 --> 00:42:16,201
Oh, bite me.

1192
00:42:16,201 --> 00:42:17,723
It's fun.

1193
00:42:17,723 --> 00:42:19,191
- Thank you, Frankie.

1194
00:42:19,191 --> 00:42:21,595
Now, Joely, you and your scaredy-bots,

1195
00:42:21,595 --> 00:42:25,453
up great, deep, drafts of the second half

1196
00:42:25,453 --> 00:42:28,698
of this stink-burger, called
The Castle of Fu Manchu.

1197
00:42:28,698 --> 00:42:30,046
Ain't that a man?

1198
00:42:30,046 --> 00:42:31,168
(buzzing)
(yelling)

1199
00:42:31,168 --> 00:42:32,944
- We've got movie siren!

1200
00:42:32,944 --> 00:42:34,527
Let's hit it, boys!

1201
00:42:43,785 --> 00:42:44,618
(crying)

1202
00:42:44,618 --> 00:42:45,785
Oh, it's okay.

1203
00:42:50,661 --> 00:42:52,322
- In two copies.

1204
00:42:52,322 --> 00:42:53,243
- [Servo] Two coffees?

1205
00:42:53,243 --> 00:42:55,243
(cries)

1206
00:42:56,408 --> 00:43:01,214
- I know you will be able to
follow, without any trouble.

1207
00:43:01,214 --> 00:43:02,456
Goodbye, Melnik.

1208
00:43:02,456 --> 00:43:03,417
- [Crow] But I'm not leaving.

1209
00:43:03,417 --> 00:43:04,405
Oh, I see.

1210
00:43:04,405 --> 00:43:06,568
You don't have to knock me over the head.

1211
00:43:06,568 --> 00:43:07,449
- Lieutenant, sir?

1212
00:43:07,449 --> 00:43:08,282
- [Servo] I feel a little bit better.

1213
00:43:08,282 --> 00:43:09,265
- [Man] Go away.

1214
00:43:09,265 --> 00:43:10,547
- [Joel] Order lunch.

1215
00:43:10,547 --> 00:43:11,882
That'll take a while.

1216
00:43:11,882 --> 00:43:12,715
- [Servo] Thanks, guys.

1217
00:43:12,715 --> 00:43:13,965
- [Man] Oh, go.

1218
00:43:15,514 --> 00:43:19,800
- [Servo] What, do you need a
ton of bricks to fall on ya?

1219
00:43:19,800 --> 00:43:21,467
- Goodbye, Sergeant.

1220
00:43:23,971 --> 00:43:25,589
(yells)

1221
00:43:25,589 --> 00:43:27,992
- [Servo] Meanwhile, in east Dubuque.

1222
00:43:27,992 --> 00:43:29,742
- [Joel] It's Nessie!

1223
00:43:33,413 --> 00:43:34,254
- It's the Boss!

1224
00:43:34,254 --> 00:43:35,135
It's Springsteen!

1225
00:43:35,135 --> 00:43:37,325
- [Man] A boat approaches!

1226
00:43:37,325 --> 00:43:38,687
- [Servo] But keep it quiet!

1227
00:43:38,687 --> 00:43:41,237
We got a super secret plan!

1228
00:43:41,237 --> 00:43:42,070
(laughs)

1229
00:43:42,070 --> 00:43:44,428
- Methinks the King approaches.

1230
00:43:44,428 --> 00:43:47,555
- [Joel] Oh, darn escalator's out again.

1231
00:43:47,555 --> 00:43:50,359
Got trapped on there once.

1232
00:43:50,359 --> 00:43:52,428
- [Man] Lin Tang arrives
with the prisoners.

1233
00:43:52,428 --> 00:43:53,643
- They could use an extension line.

1234
00:43:53,643 --> 00:43:55,793
- [Fu Manchu] Very well.

1235
00:43:55,793 --> 00:43:58,626
- [Joel] I'm done tanning, thanks.

1236
00:43:59,611 --> 00:44:02,509
- [Servo] Under this robe, I'm
naked as the day I was born.

1237
00:44:02,509 --> 00:44:03,430
Riding free and easy.

1238
00:44:03,430 --> 00:44:04,698
(laughs)

1239
00:44:04,698 --> 00:44:05,531
- You don't think there's much chance

1240
00:44:05,531 --> 00:44:06,848
he'll fall down those stairs?

1241
00:44:06,848 --> 00:44:08,223
- [Servo] No.

1242
00:44:08,223 --> 00:44:09,465
Wishful thinking.

1243
00:44:09,465 --> 00:44:13,003
(boat engine whirring)

1244
00:44:13,003 --> 00:44:14,670
- [Joel] Hi-kee-bah.

1245
00:44:17,796 --> 00:44:21,379
- [Servo] Suddenly, I
have the urge to, um.

1246
00:44:22,766 --> 00:44:24,933
- What are you looking at?

1247
00:44:26,557 --> 00:44:29,974
- [Joel] We'll be right back, after this.

1248
00:44:31,818 --> 00:44:33,020
- Come back here!

1249
00:44:33,020 --> 00:44:34,048
(grunts)

1250
00:44:34,048 --> 00:44:34,902
Where are you going?

1251
00:44:34,902 --> 00:44:36,051
- To Scarborough Fair?

1252
00:44:36,051 --> 00:44:37,252
- I must see your master.

1253
00:44:37,252 --> 00:44:39,252
- [Man] Get out of here!

1254
00:44:40,533 --> 00:44:41,366
- [Joel] That guy's gonna be

1255
00:44:41,366 --> 00:44:44,033
a sophomore for five years, man.

1256
00:44:46,203 --> 00:44:47,872
- I bring you valuable information.

1257
00:44:47,872 --> 00:44:50,009
- [Servo] I bring tidings of great joy.

1258
00:44:50,009 --> 00:44:51,838
- It's all lined up.

1259
00:44:51,838 --> 00:44:53,213
- [Omar] Start talking then --

1260
00:44:53,213 --> 00:44:54,989
- [Servo] And start chalking.

1261
00:44:54,989 --> 00:44:58,487
- [Joel] Well, once upon a
time, there were three bears.

1262
00:44:58,487 --> 00:45:00,556
- [Servo] Cher's getting
back with Gregg Allman.

1263
00:45:00,556 --> 00:45:01,544
(gasps)

1264
00:45:01,544 --> 00:45:03,680
- Lin Tang was here today, in Istanbul.

1265
00:45:03,680 --> 00:45:05,830
She took two prisoners away with her.

1266
00:45:05,830 --> 00:45:08,343
- [Joel] Justine Bateman
has a new movie coming out.

1267
00:45:08,343 --> 00:45:09,260
- Yes, yes.

1268
00:45:10,145 --> 00:45:11,427
Of course, I do not know who,

1269
00:45:11,427 --> 00:45:14,010
but I know which way they went.

1270
00:45:17,088 --> 00:45:18,171
- Well?

1271
00:45:18,171 --> 00:45:19,852
(breathing heavily)

1272
00:45:19,852 --> 00:45:24,214
- The same road Lisa took,
Master, to the other side.

1273
00:45:24,214 --> 00:45:25,047
(kiss smacks)

1274
00:45:25,047 --> 00:45:27,441
- [Joel] You smell like a fresh cookie.

1275
00:45:27,441 --> 00:45:29,101
- To Anatolia.

1276
00:45:29,101 --> 00:45:31,260
- [Crow] You're dripping sweat on me.

1277
00:45:31,260 --> 00:45:32,093
- Ahmet!

1278
00:45:34,130 --> 00:45:34,963
Reward him.

1279
00:45:34,963 --> 00:45:39,124
- [Joel] Oh, someone's got an oily t-zone.

1280
00:45:39,124 --> 00:45:39,957
- [Servo] Where's his reward?

1281
00:45:39,957 --> 00:45:41,040
(screams)

1282
00:45:41,040 --> 00:45:43,463
No, no, I meant give him a slice of pie.

1283
00:45:43,463 --> 00:45:45,653
- I'm so wasted, I forgot what he said.

1284
00:45:45,653 --> 00:45:46,486
- [Servo] A waste.

1285
00:45:46,486 --> 00:45:48,069
- [Crow] No, never.

1286
00:45:51,984 --> 00:45:55,401
- [Joel] Oh, it's the Istanbul Orkin man.

1287
00:45:58,459 --> 00:46:00,094
- [Servo] I'd say this
movie has less action than

1288
00:46:00,094 --> 00:46:02,261
a Who's Life Is It Anyway?

1289
00:46:03,135 --> 00:46:04,203
- [Joel] I'm a sailor.

1290
00:46:04,203 --> 00:46:05,036
(laughs)

1291
00:46:05,036 --> 00:46:06,619
- Will you help me?

1292
00:46:07,648 --> 00:46:09,637
(ominous music)

1293
00:46:09,637 --> 00:46:10,986
- [Servo] What, what?

1294
00:46:10,986 --> 00:46:11,819
What?

1295
00:46:12,695 --> 00:46:14,019
- [Joel] No.

1296
00:46:14,019 --> 00:46:15,568
No!

1297
00:46:15,568 --> 00:46:16,401
No!

1298
00:46:16,401 --> 00:46:17,234
Oh.

1299
00:46:19,948 --> 00:46:23,927
- [Servo] Michael Caine and
Nancy Kulp are vampires.

1300
00:46:23,927 --> 00:46:26,094
- [Joel] Shoot, roommates!

1301
00:46:27,972 --> 00:46:30,555
- David Bowie, from The Hunger.

1302
00:46:32,124 --> 00:46:34,154
- [Servo] And he's all dewy.

1303
00:46:34,154 --> 00:46:35,182
Dewy Bowie.

1304
00:46:35,182 --> 00:46:37,182
- [Joel] I hate jet lag.

1305
00:46:39,388 --> 00:46:42,085
- Boy, I really racked up the
frequent flyer miles though.

1306
00:46:42,085 --> 00:46:43,540
- [Servo] Yeah, frequent dyer miles.

1307
00:46:43,540 --> 00:46:44,998
(laughs)

1308
00:46:44,998 --> 00:46:45,962
- [Joel] Dece.

1309
00:46:45,962 --> 00:46:46,950
You're feelin' better.

1310
00:46:46,950 --> 00:46:48,873
- [Servo] A little.

1311
00:46:48,873 --> 00:46:50,502
- Kessler!

1312
00:46:50,502 --> 00:46:51,823
Ingrid!

1313
00:46:51,823 --> 00:46:53,406
- [Servo] In color.

1314
00:46:55,855 --> 00:46:58,512
- She's kinda overdressed for espionage.

1315
00:46:58,512 --> 00:47:00,262
- Professor Heracles.

1316
00:47:02,376 --> 00:47:04,187
(heavy breathing)

1317
00:47:04,187 --> 00:47:07,298
- [Joel] She had to sit
next to the stinky guy.

1318
00:47:07,298 --> 00:47:09,381
(laughs)

1319
00:47:10,342 --> 00:47:12,465
- [Servo] Oh, I can't watch this.

1320
00:47:12,465 --> 00:47:14,548
I mean, I can't see this.

1321
00:47:16,110 --> 00:47:19,100
- [Joel] It's kinda like a
Metallica video, but slower.

1322
00:47:19,100 --> 00:47:21,624
- [Servo] Oh, come on, what
is this, Kirlian photography?

1323
00:47:21,624 --> 00:47:24,393
- Yeah, Moe, Larry, and
Kirlian photography.

1324
00:47:24,393 --> 00:47:26,289
(laughs)

1325
00:47:26,289 --> 00:47:28,692
- Geez, and I thought City of
Hope was an underlit movie.

1326
00:47:28,692 --> 00:47:30,775
(groans)

1327
00:47:33,125 --> 00:47:35,448
They've been candied.

1328
00:47:35,448 --> 00:47:36,316
Candide?

1329
00:47:36,316 --> 00:47:37,149
- [Servo] Candide.

1330
00:47:37,149 --> 00:47:38,359
- Where are we?

1331
00:47:38,359 --> 00:47:40,343
- [Joel] You're one step away
from never working again.

1332
00:47:40,343 --> 00:47:41,260
- Anatolia.

1333
00:47:42,386 --> 00:47:44,136
He had a boss for us.

1334
00:47:45,884 --> 00:47:48,634
- They've turned us into Warhols.

1335
00:47:50,317 --> 00:47:52,640
- It's incredible.

1336
00:47:52,640 --> 00:47:54,002
Who were those people?

1337
00:47:54,002 --> 00:47:55,577
- [Joel] Who are these people?

1338
00:47:55,577 --> 00:47:59,494
- They were kidnapped,
by the men of Fu Manchu.

1339
00:48:01,852 --> 00:48:02,769
- Fu Man --

1340
00:48:03,668 --> 00:48:04,501
- Manchu.

1341
00:48:04,501 --> 00:48:05,965
Spit it out, honey.

1342
00:48:05,965 --> 00:48:09,215
- I can't move, but feel I'm paralyzed.

1343
00:48:11,492 --> 00:48:14,483
- You'll be alright in a few minutes.

1344
00:48:14,483 --> 00:48:17,316
They used my crystals against you.

1345
00:48:18,568 --> 00:48:19,450
- [Servo] This is the first color movie

1346
00:48:19,450 --> 00:48:21,599
that needs to be colorized.

1347
00:48:21,599 --> 00:48:22,432
(laughs)

1348
00:48:22,432 --> 00:48:24,265
- But in a small dose.

1349
00:48:26,099 --> 00:48:26,932
(groans)

1350
00:48:26,932 --> 00:48:27,765
- Professor!

1351
00:48:27,765 --> 00:48:28,598
- [Joel] Look, you're overtired.

1352
00:48:28,598 --> 00:48:29,824
We'll talk to you later.

1353
00:48:29,824 --> 00:48:31,907
(laughs)

1354
00:48:34,417 --> 00:48:35,658
- She could use a good clay pack.

1355
00:48:35,658 --> 00:48:36,820
- [Joel] Mm-hmm.

1356
00:48:36,820 --> 00:48:37,653
Spores.

1357
00:48:39,333 --> 00:48:40,833
- [Servo] Come on.

1358
00:48:42,991 --> 00:48:45,491
Meanwhile, in downtown Duluth.

1359
00:48:46,503 --> 00:48:47,544
- [Joel] It's not funny.

1360
00:48:47,544 --> 00:48:48,692
- [Servo] I went to Istanbul,

1361
00:48:48,692 --> 00:48:50,949
and all I got was this lousy fez, huh?

1362
00:48:50,949 --> 00:48:51,782
(laughs)

1363
00:48:51,782 --> 00:48:52,724
It's funny.

1364
00:48:52,724 --> 00:48:54,513
- Hey, take a long walk off that thing.

1365
00:48:54,513 --> 00:48:55,763
- [Servo] Yeah.

1366
00:48:59,827 --> 00:49:01,403
- [Joel] Hi, we're the Boatniks.

1367
00:49:01,403 --> 00:49:03,486
(laughs)

1368
00:49:07,491 --> 00:49:08,479
- Inspector Ahmet?

1369
00:49:08,479 --> 00:49:09,507
- [Crow] You inspect her, I'm busy.

1370
00:49:09,507 --> 00:49:10,829
- Told that we'd expect you here.

1371
00:49:10,829 --> 00:49:14,875
- An honor, sir, but I'm
afraid that I have bad news.

1372
00:49:14,875 --> 00:49:16,316
- What is the bad news, Inspector?

1373
00:49:16,316 --> 00:49:17,149
- [Servo] My hat.

1374
00:49:17,149 --> 00:49:19,040
- The bandits, who attacked the castle,

1375
00:49:19,040 --> 00:49:21,430
were Omar Pasha's men.

1376
00:49:21,430 --> 00:49:22,699
- Omar Pasha?

1377
00:49:22,699 --> 00:49:24,888
- [Inspector] He controls the opium trade.

1378
00:49:24,888 --> 00:49:26,063
- Opium?
- [Crow] The perfume?

1379
00:49:26,063 --> 00:49:30,230
- An informer called Melnik,
appeared this morning, killed.

1380
00:49:31,257 --> 00:49:32,090
(buzzing)

1381
00:49:32,090 --> 00:49:33,126
- [Servo] Tell me again, please.

1382
00:49:33,126 --> 00:49:34,102
I need your help, please.

1383
00:49:34,102 --> 00:49:35,086
- His last visit, yesterday,

1384
00:49:35,086 --> 00:49:37,753
was to Omar Pasha's coffee shop.

1385
00:49:38,785 --> 00:49:41,148
♫ Omar Pasha ♫

1386
00:49:41,148 --> 00:49:42,390
(laughs)

1387
00:49:42,390 --> 00:49:44,793
- [Inspector] I should
have listened to him.

1388
00:49:44,793 --> 00:49:45,914
- Why?

1389
00:49:45,914 --> 00:49:48,081
- Omar Pasha has vanished.

1390
00:49:49,586 --> 00:49:51,589
- Meanwhile, in, oh, forget it.

1391
00:49:51,589 --> 00:49:52,483
(sighs)

1392
00:49:52,483 --> 00:49:53,658
- [Voiceover] That he
has gone to Anatolia,

1393
00:49:53,658 --> 00:49:57,423
to rescue the girl, Lisa, and
is camped opposite the castle,

1394
00:49:57,423 --> 00:49:58,425
on the other side of the --

1395
00:49:58,425 --> 00:50:01,963
- [Joel] Looks like two seals
waterskiing, doesn't it?

1396
00:50:01,963 --> 00:50:03,044
- [Crow] Uh-huh.
- [Joel] Kind of?

1397
00:50:03,044 --> 00:50:04,259
- [Crow] No.

1398
00:50:04,259 --> 00:50:06,596
(singing in foreign language)

1399
00:50:06,596 --> 00:50:10,763
♫ Oh, lord, it's hard to be humble ♫

1400
00:50:14,086 --> 00:50:15,419
- [Servo] Uh-oh.

1401
00:50:18,532 --> 00:50:20,468
- Hey, it's the grand wizard himself.

1402
00:50:20,468 --> 00:50:22,635
- [Joel] What a burn, wow.

1403
00:50:24,425 --> 00:50:25,258
(thud)

1404
00:50:25,258 --> 00:50:27,849
(yells)

1405
00:50:27,849 --> 00:50:28,682
- Come on!

1406
00:50:28,682 --> 00:50:29,515
- [Servo] Thank you, thank you.

1407
00:50:29,515 --> 00:50:30,348
Next show at 10 o'clock.

1408
00:50:30,348 --> 00:50:32,682
Thank you very much.

1409
00:50:32,682 --> 00:50:34,485
- [Joel] Hey, don't step on the guy.

1410
00:50:34,485 --> 00:50:36,568
(laughs)

1411
00:50:38,183 --> 00:50:39,016
Come on.

1412
00:50:39,016 --> 00:50:40,872
- [Man] All is clear, master.

1413
00:50:40,872 --> 00:50:45,161
- [Servo] Oh, geez, I thought
Shriners helped people.

1414
00:50:45,161 --> 00:50:47,364
- [Joel] Rock the Casbah, dude.

1415
00:50:47,364 --> 00:50:50,194
- [Servo] Sharif don't like it.

1416
00:50:50,194 --> 00:50:52,264
- Wouldn't it be great
if we knew who they were,

1417
00:50:52,264 --> 00:50:54,721
where they are, or what they were doing?

1418
00:50:54,721 --> 00:50:55,615
- [Servo] Pretty much.

1419
00:50:55,615 --> 00:50:59,116
- [Joel] Well, he looks
like a Century 21 salesman.

1420
00:50:59,116 --> 00:51:01,920
- [Crow] Gandhi's back, and he's stuffed.

1421
00:51:01,920 --> 00:51:02,920
- Fu Manchu.

1422
00:51:04,483 --> 00:51:06,700
- [Fu Manchu] Bring
forth the two prisoners,

1423
00:51:06,700 --> 00:51:09,279
Dr. Kessler and Dr. Ingrid Cox.

1424
00:51:09,279 --> 00:51:10,481
- [Lin Tang] Yes, father.

1425
00:51:10,481 --> 00:51:11,883
The guards are bringing them.

1426
00:51:11,883 --> 00:51:14,006
- [Servo] Oh, look, it's the
original hand-hammered wok.

1427
00:51:14,006 --> 00:51:15,621
- It looks like stainless steel from here.

1428
00:51:15,621 --> 00:51:18,371
- [Servo] Oh, yeah, you're right.

1429
00:51:20,414 --> 00:51:21,247
- [Joel] Love me.

1430
00:51:21,247 --> 00:51:23,485
- [Fu Manchu] I have brought
you here to save the life

1431
00:51:23,485 --> 00:51:25,969
of someone, whose knowledge I require,

1432
00:51:25,969 --> 00:51:28,412
as a thirsty man needs water.

1433
00:51:28,412 --> 00:51:29,667
- [Crow] Tonight on, You Asked For It.

1434
00:51:29,667 --> 00:51:31,950
- Crystal clear water, Dr. Kessler.

1435
00:51:31,950 --> 00:51:34,620
- [Joel] Crystal blue persuasion.

1436
00:51:34,620 --> 00:51:36,329
- [Servo] Ah, cripes, this again.

1437
00:51:36,329 --> 00:51:37,603
- The name of the person to whom

1438
00:51:37,603 --> 00:51:40,186
I refer, is Professor Heracles.

1439
00:51:44,439 --> 00:51:45,935
- [Servo] Uh, we're underwhelmed.

1440
00:51:45,935 --> 00:51:48,018
(laughs)

1441
00:51:50,060 --> 00:51:51,622
You know, Burt Young has looked worse.

1442
00:51:51,622 --> 00:51:52,955
- [Joel] Mm-hmm.

1443
00:51:56,843 --> 00:51:59,553
- Well, he's Burt Young alright.

1444
00:51:59,553 --> 00:52:00,885
- [Dr. Kessler] He is dying.

1445
00:52:00,885 --> 00:52:02,058
- [Ingrid] Professor.

1446
00:52:02,058 --> 00:52:03,206
- You will use your skill, doctor.

1447
00:52:03,206 --> 00:52:04,755
You will make him live.

1448
00:52:04,755 --> 00:52:05,588
- [Crow] Dammit, fool!

1449
00:52:05,588 --> 00:52:06,838
I'm a surgeon, not a doctor.

1450
00:52:06,838 --> 00:52:09,495
- I am not a miracle worker.

1451
00:52:09,495 --> 00:52:13,981
Besides, you took everything
away, except my hands.

1452
00:52:13,981 --> 00:52:16,104
- On the contrary, Dr. Kessler --

1453
00:52:16,104 --> 00:52:18,654
- [Servo] Et cetera, et cetera, et cetera.

1454
00:52:18,654 --> 00:52:22,821
- You will find everything
here, that you require.

1455
00:52:24,128 --> 00:52:27,760
- [Joel] Let's see what's
behind door number one.

1456
00:52:27,760 --> 00:52:28,843
- [Crow] Ooh.

1457
00:52:33,821 --> 00:52:35,517
- [Servo] Here, I have
everything you need.

1458
00:52:35,517 --> 00:52:37,680
I threw in the hairy,
naked man, just for kicks.

1459
00:52:37,680 --> 00:52:39,347
- [Joel] Nice touch.

1460
00:52:41,231 --> 00:52:42,366
- [Dr. Kessler] What's
wrong with that man?

1461
00:52:42,366 --> 00:52:43,434
- [Crow] Nothing at all.

1462
00:52:43,434 --> 00:52:45,103
- [Fu Manchu] There is nothing
wrong with him, doctor.

1463
00:52:45,103 --> 00:52:47,160
He is in perfect physical condition.

1464
00:52:47,160 --> 00:52:48,161
- [Joel] I'll say.

1465
00:52:48,161 --> 00:52:50,070
- And unlike Professor Heracles,

1466
00:52:50,070 --> 00:52:52,193
his heart is as sound as a bell.

1467
00:52:52,193 --> 00:52:53,315
- [Servo] Bong.

1468
00:52:53,315 --> 00:52:56,163
- Do you not agree, doctor,
that Professor Heracles

1469
00:52:56,163 --> 00:52:59,336
should have that splendid heart?

1470
00:52:59,336 --> 00:53:02,919
- [Joel] If it comes
with that beefy chest.

1471
00:53:03,942 --> 00:53:06,159
- [Dr. Kessler] But that
man is not dead or dying.

1472
00:53:06,159 --> 00:53:07,400
- [Crow] He's only mostly dead!

1473
00:53:07,400 --> 00:53:08,233
- He is drugged.

1474
00:53:08,233 --> 00:53:11,475
He will die for the sake of science.

1475
00:53:11,475 --> 00:53:13,919
- And for your sake, also.

1476
00:53:13,919 --> 00:53:16,442
- I need Heracles to complete my plans.

1477
00:53:16,442 --> 00:53:19,526
I need him alive, conscious, coherent --

1478
00:53:19,526 --> 00:53:21,516
- [Servo] I wish this movie
were conscious or coherent!

1479
00:53:21,516 --> 00:53:23,516
(cries)

1480
00:53:25,414 --> 00:53:26,581
- If I refuse?

1481
00:53:27,657 --> 00:53:29,019
- I hadn't thought of that.

1482
00:53:29,019 --> 00:53:30,154
Gosh, he's clever.

1483
00:53:30,154 --> 00:53:35,068
- Then Dr. Ingrid Cox will die
an extremely painful death.

1484
00:53:35,068 --> 00:53:36,162
- No!

1485
00:53:36,162 --> 00:53:39,662
- [Joel] No fresh ground pepper with that?

1486
00:53:40,782 --> 00:53:43,813
- The choice is yours, Dr. Kessler.

1487
00:53:43,813 --> 00:53:45,682
- [Servo] Well?

1488
00:53:45,682 --> 00:53:49,849
- In order to convince you, I
shall arrange a demonstration.

1489
00:53:53,226 --> 00:53:54,294
- No!

1490
00:53:54,294 --> 00:53:55,711
- [Servo] No, no.

1491
00:53:59,180 --> 00:54:00,013
What's goin' on?

1492
00:54:00,013 --> 00:54:02,846
- Glenn Manning, get off that dam!

1493
00:54:03,867 --> 00:54:05,269
- [Joel] Bridge on the River Kwai.

1494
00:54:05,269 --> 00:54:09,052
- [Servo] Looks like it, doesn't it?

1495
00:54:09,052 --> 00:54:10,543
- [Joel] Biggest crack by a dam site.

1496
00:54:10,543 --> 00:54:11,464
(laughs)

1497
00:54:11,464 --> 00:54:13,039
Yep, right there.

1498
00:54:13,039 --> 00:54:13,872
- Hey, there's a little Dutch boy

1499
00:54:13,872 --> 00:54:14,705
putting his finger in there.

1500
00:54:14,705 --> 00:54:16,038
- [Servo] Where?

1501
00:54:17,512 --> 00:54:18,366
- [Man] Run!

1502
00:54:18,366 --> 00:54:19,702
Run for you lives!

1503
00:54:19,702 --> 00:54:21,157
- [Servo] Run men!

1504
00:54:21,157 --> 00:54:22,919
- [Joel] The plot's
starting to make sense.

1505
00:54:22,919 --> 00:54:23,752
Run!

1506
00:54:29,982 --> 00:54:31,344
- [Servo] This dam scene.

1507
00:54:31,344 --> 00:54:34,282
- Hey, don't forget to punch out!

1508
00:54:34,282 --> 00:54:38,449
- [Joel] You know, I suddenly
have to go to the bathroom.

1509
00:54:39,435 --> 00:54:40,268
- [Crow] Really?

1510
00:54:40,268 --> 00:54:41,101
- [Joel] Yep.

1511
00:54:41,101 --> 00:54:42,696
- [Servo] Why, I wonder?

1512
00:54:42,696 --> 00:54:44,696
- [Joel] Funniest thing.

1513
00:54:47,692 --> 00:54:48,525
- You know, they might need some

1514
00:54:48,525 --> 00:54:50,215
Thompson's WaterSeal up there.

1515
00:54:50,215 --> 00:54:52,498
- [Servo] I think
something to hold it back.

1516
00:54:52,498 --> 00:54:53,713
Don't worry, men!

1517
00:54:53,713 --> 00:54:57,625
It's the Egyptians who are gonna get us!

1518
00:54:57,625 --> 00:54:59,014
Pharaoh and the gang.

1519
00:54:59,014 --> 00:55:01,264
(clicking)

1520
00:55:03,807 --> 00:55:06,224
Yay, we're getting off early!

1521
00:55:08,160 --> 00:55:08,993
Free day.

1522
00:55:10,825 --> 00:55:12,825
- Force 10 from Navarone

1523
00:55:13,802 --> 00:55:15,004
- [Joel] Oh, quit grovelling.

1524
00:55:15,004 --> 00:55:16,085
- [Servo] Gravelling.

1525
00:55:16,085 --> 00:55:18,418
(screaming)

1526
00:55:20,385 --> 00:55:21,466
Uh-huh.

1527
00:55:21,466 --> 00:55:22,761
Yep, yep.

1528
00:55:22,761 --> 00:55:23,803
You know, cutting it faster

1529
00:55:23,803 --> 00:55:26,636
doesn't make it any more exciting.

1530
00:55:28,262 --> 00:55:29,262
- [Crow] Ah.

1531
00:55:30,348 --> 00:55:31,763
- [Servo] Oh, that's a relief.

1532
00:55:31,763 --> 00:55:33,234
- [Joel] I didn't think
that dam would ever break.

1533
00:55:33,234 --> 00:55:34,567
- [Servo] Uh-uh.

1534
00:55:37,013 --> 00:55:38,930
Oh, the Rolling Stones.

1535
00:55:39,883 --> 00:55:42,380
Doesn't do much for me.

1536
00:55:42,380 --> 00:55:44,630
(rumbling)

1537
00:55:47,040 --> 00:55:49,310
It's kind of convulsive, isn't it?

1538
00:55:49,310 --> 00:55:50,143
(laughs)

1539
00:55:50,143 --> 00:55:52,583
- You have got to be kidding me.

1540
00:55:52,583 --> 00:55:53,785
- [Servo] This isn't very good.

1541
00:55:53,785 --> 00:55:55,868
- [Joel] Prince of Tides.

1542
00:56:03,412 --> 00:56:07,751
- The River, with Mel
Gibson and Sissy Spacek.

1543
00:56:07,751 --> 00:56:10,394
- [Joel] You know, I miss
the water slide at the Dells.

1544
00:56:10,394 --> 00:56:12,504
- [Servo] I wonder.

1545
00:56:12,504 --> 00:56:15,254
Oh, look, rock made out of water.

1546
00:56:20,969 --> 00:56:22,157
- Complete annihilation.

1547
00:56:22,157 --> 00:56:23,813
- I am the god of hydrotherapy.

1548
00:56:23,813 --> 00:56:27,538
- Even Nayland Smith cannot
touch you now, father.

1549
00:56:27,538 --> 00:56:29,788
- I wish that he would try.

1550
00:56:30,862 --> 00:56:31,695
(dramatic music)

1551
00:56:31,695 --> 00:56:35,375
- [Joel] We'll be back,
after these messages.

1552
00:56:35,375 --> 00:56:39,292
- [Servo] Meanwhile, in
Two Harbors, Minnesota.

1553
00:56:41,477 --> 00:56:42,892
You must kill Kurtz.

1554
00:56:42,892 --> 00:56:45,642
Terminate with extreme prejudice.

1555
00:56:48,326 --> 00:56:50,315
- I wish this film had some news for me.

1556
00:56:50,315 --> 00:56:52,482
(mumbles)

1557
00:56:54,454 --> 00:56:55,704
- This is Asia.

1558
00:56:56,667 --> 00:56:59,194
- [Servo] Could we see
specific sites in Asia?

1559
00:56:59,194 --> 00:57:01,130
- [Inspector] I must leave you, gentlemen.

1560
00:57:01,130 --> 00:57:03,627
- Thank you, Inspector, for all your help.

1561
00:57:03,627 --> 00:57:06,180
I'm sorry, Petrie, but
this is where we part.

1562
00:57:06,180 --> 00:57:07,421
- Speaking of part, comb that hair.

1563
00:57:07,421 --> 00:57:08,369
- It's better that way.

1564
00:57:08,369 --> 00:57:10,399
You can be of more use to me in Istanbul.

1565
00:57:10,399 --> 00:57:12,415
- [Joel] Stuffed on a mantel.
- [Petrie] How?

1566
00:57:12,415 --> 00:57:13,782
- I want you to telegraph the

1567
00:57:13,782 --> 00:57:16,039
Home Secretary's office in London.

1568
00:57:16,039 --> 00:57:16,872
- [Petrie] Mm-hmm.

1569
00:57:16,872 --> 00:57:17,705
- Use the standard code.

1570
00:57:17,705 --> 00:57:19,029
Tell them that I intend to try

1571
00:57:19,029 --> 00:57:21,740
to get into Fu Manchu's castle.

1572
00:57:21,740 --> 00:57:24,730
- But how do you know that Fu
Manchu captured the castle?

1573
00:57:24,730 --> 00:57:27,134
Besides, there's nothing
but guesswork to go on.

1574
00:57:27,134 --> 00:57:28,789
- I have something here --

1575
00:57:28,789 --> 00:57:31,789
- [Joel] Wait, that's Robert Goulet!

1576
00:57:33,356 --> 00:57:36,413
- This was found on a dead man --

1577
00:57:36,413 --> 00:57:38,496
(groans)

1578
00:57:39,804 --> 00:57:42,224
- Still guesswork, Petrie?

1579
00:57:42,224 --> 00:57:43,057
- [Joel] Dish?

1580
00:57:43,057 --> 00:57:43,890
- Kessler's head cloth!

1581
00:57:43,890 --> 00:57:46,057
(mumbles)

1582
00:57:48,940 --> 00:57:50,715
- [Ingrid] Curt, you mustn't do this.

1583
00:57:50,715 --> 00:57:51,548
- [Servo] Oh, well.

1584
00:57:51,548 --> 00:57:52,381
Very well, then.

1585
00:57:52,381 --> 00:57:54,214
I will use the toilet.

1586
00:57:58,326 --> 00:57:59,159
- Well, can't be that bad.

1587
00:57:59,159 --> 00:58:00,718
They put them in the same cell.

1588
00:58:00,718 --> 00:58:01,551
- [Servo] Yeah.

1589
00:58:01,551 --> 00:58:05,151
- A doctor can't say no to saving a life.

1590
00:58:05,151 --> 00:58:07,674
- [Joel] Except when the
patient has no insurance.

1591
00:58:07,674 --> 00:58:08,796
- You cannot do this.

1592
00:58:08,796 --> 00:58:10,852
If by saving Professor Heracles' life,

1593
00:58:10,852 --> 00:58:14,043
you are helping this
murderer in his plans.

1594
00:58:14,043 --> 00:58:15,110
- [Servo] Classic tragedy, eh?

1595
00:58:15,110 --> 00:58:16,115
- Do you believe that Fu Manchu

1596
00:58:16,115 --> 00:58:19,627
will let Heracles live,
after he's used him?

1597
00:58:19,627 --> 00:58:20,495
- I don't know.

1598
00:58:20,495 --> 00:58:24,353
- [Crow] Much about that,
but I know what I like.

1599
00:58:24,353 --> 00:58:27,464
- But we have to try everything.

1600
00:58:27,464 --> 00:58:31,750
Nobody before tried to
do such an operation.

1601
00:58:31,750 --> 00:58:33,913
- [Joel] You mean the goofy
game for dopey doctors?

1602
00:58:33,913 --> 00:58:35,080
- [Servo] Yep.

1603
00:58:35,942 --> 00:58:36,775
- Do you --

1604
00:58:36,775 --> 00:58:37,812
- Love me?

1605
00:58:37,812 --> 00:58:38,920
- [Servo] Do I what?

1606
00:58:38,920 --> 00:58:41,296
- Do you think you can do it?

1607
00:58:41,296 --> 00:58:42,129
- [Servo] In the road.

1608
00:58:42,129 --> 00:58:42,962
- Yes.

1609
00:58:42,962 --> 00:58:46,379
(groans)
- [Servo] Sorry.

1610
00:58:48,453 --> 00:58:49,588
- [Dr. Kessler] Yes, I know we can do it.

1611
00:58:49,588 --> 00:58:51,978
- [Joel] Now that's lipstick
that lasts, from Yardley.

1612
00:58:51,978 --> 00:58:52,811
- [Servo] Mm-hmm.

1613
00:58:52,811 --> 00:58:54,715
- [Kessler] I hope.

1614
00:58:54,715 --> 00:58:56,132
- I'm so ashamed.

1615
00:58:58,520 --> 00:59:00,402
- Are you sure --

1616
00:59:00,402 --> 00:59:01,404
- [Joel] Bees can fly?

1617
00:59:01,404 --> 00:59:05,571
- You're not doing all this
for me, just to save my life?

1618
00:59:07,358 --> 00:59:08,226
- [Servo] Well, look.

1619
00:59:08,226 --> 00:59:09,441
I just wanted to get to first base

1620
00:59:09,441 --> 00:59:12,108
with you, and things snowballed.

1621
00:59:13,182 --> 00:59:14,015
- What?

1622
00:59:14,015 --> 00:59:14,848
Oh, were you talking?

1623
00:59:14,848 --> 00:59:15,681
Sorry.

1624
00:59:15,681 --> 00:59:17,375
- [Kessler] We have not a chance.

1625
00:59:17,375 --> 00:59:19,030
In this moment --

1626
00:59:19,030 --> 00:59:19,863
- [Joel] You know, it's kind of like

1627
00:59:19,863 --> 00:59:23,159
watching the Hollywood Squares.

1628
00:59:23,159 --> 00:59:25,268
- [Kessler] Who matters to me.

1629
00:59:25,268 --> 00:59:27,378
- [Servo] You are every
woman in the world, to me.

1630
00:59:27,378 --> 00:59:29,941
(footsteps)

1631
00:59:29,941 --> 00:59:31,317
- [Crow] Have you been
listening the whole time?

1632
00:59:31,317 --> 00:59:33,119
I thought this was a private cell.

1633
00:59:33,119 --> 00:59:33,952
Sneaky.

1634
00:59:33,952 --> 00:59:35,368
- [Servo] This scene is a real strain.

1635
00:59:35,368 --> 00:59:36,201
(laughs)

1636
00:59:36,201 --> 00:59:38,241
- [Crow] That's grate though, just grate.

1637
00:59:38,241 --> 00:59:39,324
- [Servo] No.

1638
00:59:42,276 --> 00:59:43,651
- Yes, we know how long this has been on!

1639
00:59:43,651 --> 00:59:46,244
Don't shove it in our face!

1640
00:59:46,244 --> 00:59:50,244
- [Joel] Tonight, on a
very special Dr. Kildare.

1641
00:59:51,531 --> 00:59:53,510
- [Servo] You say ether, and I say either.

1642
00:59:53,510 --> 00:59:55,099
(laughs)

1643
00:59:55,099 --> 00:59:56,113
Let's call the whole thing off.

1644
00:59:56,113 --> 00:59:57,916
- [Joel] Breathe deep,
the gathering gloom.

1645
00:59:57,916 --> 01:00:00,583
Watch lights fade in every room.

1646
01:00:03,470 --> 01:00:04,672
- [Servo] Oh, this is aromatherapy.

1647
01:00:04,672 --> 01:00:05,753
I've seen this before.

1648
01:00:05,753 --> 01:00:06,586
(breathes deep)

1649
01:00:06,586 --> 01:00:07,436
- Yep, more, more.

1650
01:00:07,436 --> 01:00:10,319
Keep it comin', I can take more.

1651
01:00:10,319 --> 01:00:11,577
- [Servo] Don't look at me!

1652
01:00:11,577 --> 01:00:13,577
Don't look at me, mommy!

1653
01:00:16,451 --> 01:00:17,451
Frank Booth.

1654
01:00:21,938 --> 01:00:23,767
- Suzy Wong was arraigned in Los Angeles

1655
01:00:23,767 --> 01:00:27,434
County Court for
impersonating Marlo Thomas.

1656
01:00:28,761 --> 01:00:31,262
- [Joel] I am Suzy Wong.

1657
01:00:31,262 --> 01:00:33,060
- [Servo] I am Suzy Wong.

1658
01:00:33,060 --> 01:00:34,727
- No, I'm Suzy Wong.

1659
01:00:36,424 --> 01:00:37,760
- [Servo] Will the real Suzy Wong --

1660
01:00:37,760 --> 01:00:39,202
- [Joel] It's the world of Suzy Wong.

1661
01:00:39,202 --> 01:00:41,004
(laughs)

1662
01:00:41,004 --> 01:00:42,780
- Okay, who wants a drum stick?

1663
01:00:42,780 --> 01:00:43,613
(laughs)

1664
01:00:43,613 --> 01:00:45,030
I'm just kidding.

1665
01:00:47,239 --> 01:00:51,406
- [Servo] First, we split the
top, and pour in real butter.

1666
01:00:56,425 --> 01:00:57,840
(yelling)

1667
01:00:57,840 --> 01:01:00,364
- [Joel] Take it easy,
it's just tempera paint.

1668
01:01:00,364 --> 01:01:01,659
- [Crow] Okay.

1669
01:01:01,659 --> 01:01:03,915
- [Joel] Real blood
doesn't bead like that!

1670
01:01:03,915 --> 01:01:05,832
- [Crow] Using cadmium.

1671
01:01:08,188 --> 01:01:09,523
- [Servo] Did I take the Hippocratic oath?

1672
01:01:09,523 --> 01:01:11,392
- No, you took the hypocritic oath.

1673
01:01:11,392 --> 01:01:12,225
(laughs)

1674
01:01:12,225 --> 01:01:15,705
- [Servo] Oh, damn, I
thought I did that one.

1675
01:01:15,705 --> 01:01:20,391
- I'm a dermatologist, I
have no idea what I'm doing.

1676
01:01:20,391 --> 01:01:24,558
- [Joel] He's playing
hangman on this guy's belly.

1677
01:01:28,468 --> 01:01:30,100
- Well, I see by the
old clock on the wall,

1678
01:01:30,100 --> 01:01:32,597
it's time for more boredom!

1679
01:01:32,597 --> 01:01:34,306
- [Joel] I'm Harold Lloyd.

1680
01:01:34,306 --> 01:01:35,673
- [Servo] Ooh!
- [Crow] Oh!

1681
01:01:35,673 --> 01:01:37,923
- [Servo] Ooh!
- [Crow] Oh!

1682
01:01:39,644 --> 01:01:40,477
(grunts)

1683
01:01:40,477 --> 01:01:42,007
- [Servo] Ooh!
- [Crow] Oh!

1684
01:01:42,007 --> 01:01:43,877
- [Servo] Ouch.

1685
01:01:43,877 --> 01:01:45,492
- [Servo] Ooh!
- [Crow] Ow!

1686
01:01:45,492 --> 01:01:47,575
(groans)

1687
01:01:49,845 --> 01:01:51,126
(laughs)

1688
01:01:51,126 --> 01:01:52,209
Look at this shot.

1689
01:01:52,209 --> 01:01:55,506
They should never have let Shatner direct!

1690
01:01:55,506 --> 01:01:57,095
- [Joel] Sweating like Tom Jones.

1691
01:01:57,095 --> 01:01:59,512
- [Servo] That's not unusual.

1692
01:02:00,560 --> 01:02:01,770
- [Joel] What's new, pussycat?

1693
01:02:01,770 --> 01:02:02,865
- Yeah, we would you like to try this?

1694
01:02:02,865 --> 01:02:05,028
It's kind of fun.

1695
01:02:05,028 --> 01:02:09,195
- [Joel] Here, I've got to
go check on the sauce there.

1696
01:02:12,078 --> 01:02:12,946
- [Servo] Oh, don't wet the forehead.

1697
01:02:12,946 --> 01:02:14,696
The chest, the chest.

1698
01:02:16,777 --> 01:02:20,035
- What, are you carving Pinocchio?

1699
01:02:20,035 --> 01:02:22,952
(upbeat pop music)

1700
01:02:27,405 --> 01:02:30,655
- [Joel] Tap hard once, tap hard twice.

1701
01:02:32,198 --> 01:02:36,198
Oh, now you've gotta fix
what you've done wrong.

1702
01:02:38,153 --> 01:02:41,868
- What, are you clamping
every individual cell?

1703
01:02:41,868 --> 01:02:44,285
Got the whole Dremel kit out.

1704
01:02:45,846 --> 01:02:46,928
- [Joel] Man, this scene is so gross,

1705
01:02:46,928 --> 01:02:49,178
even the lighting guy left.

1706
01:02:50,012 --> 01:02:52,429
- [Servo] He left awhile ago.

1707
01:02:54,578 --> 01:02:56,167
- [Joel] Oh, please!

1708
01:02:56,167 --> 01:02:57,000
(groaning)

1709
01:02:57,000 --> 01:02:57,833
(coughs)

1710
01:02:57,833 --> 01:02:58,666
- [Servo] It's just a gizzard!

1711
01:02:58,666 --> 01:03:00,499
Save that for the cat.

1712
01:03:03,457 --> 01:03:05,124
- [Crow] Oh, Donald.

1713
01:03:11,335 --> 01:03:12,296
- [Servo] Ever operate before?

1714
01:03:12,296 --> 01:03:13,129
- Nope.

1715
01:03:14,272 --> 01:03:16,022
- [Servo] Me neither.

1716
01:03:17,156 --> 01:03:19,118
- [Joel] Ooh, his ink pen blew up.

1717
01:03:19,118 --> 01:03:20,961
- [Servo] Yeah, look at his fingers.

1718
01:03:20,961 --> 01:03:23,878
- Help me, somebody please help me.

1719
01:03:29,575 --> 01:03:30,513
- [Servo] I shouldn't have had that,

1720
01:03:30,513 --> 01:03:31,346
(gags)

1721
01:03:31,346 --> 01:03:33,179
Cobb salad, for lunch.

1722
01:03:37,789 --> 01:03:38,871
- You know, they look totally different,

1723
01:03:38,871 --> 01:03:40,633
when you open them up.

1724
01:03:40,633 --> 01:03:42,800
There's no little numbers.

1725
01:03:46,214 --> 01:03:48,778
- [Joel] You know, I am completely
off the manual right now.

1726
01:03:48,778 --> 01:03:51,261
I have no idea what I am doing.

1727
01:03:51,261 --> 01:03:52,844
It is wild in here.

1728
01:03:54,198 --> 01:03:55,696
- What you rootin' around for, tubers?

1729
01:03:55,696 --> 01:03:56,911
Close him up!

1730
01:03:56,911 --> 01:04:01,078
- [Servo] Crazy clock, a new
novel by Henry (mumbles).

1731
01:04:01,918 --> 01:04:03,501
That was fantastic.

1732
01:04:04,922 --> 01:04:05,990
You?

1733
01:04:05,990 --> 01:04:08,740
- Was it disgusting for you, too?

1734
01:04:10,757 --> 01:04:12,252
- [Servo] Kind of looks like
an Annie Leibovitz photo.

1735
01:04:12,252 --> 01:04:14,669
(kiss smack)

1736
01:04:15,924 --> 01:04:18,474
(exhales)

1737
01:04:18,474 --> 01:04:20,891
- I'm spent, I feel so empty.

1738
01:04:23,187 --> 01:04:24,749
- [Servo] Well.

1739
01:04:24,749 --> 01:04:28,141
Meanwhile, at Shakespeare In The Park.

1740
01:04:28,141 --> 01:04:29,996
Hope they're doing Macbeth!

1741
01:04:29,996 --> 01:04:30,829
- Gee, I never thought I'd be

1742
01:04:30,829 --> 01:04:33,579
grateful to see this scene again.

1743
01:04:34,726 --> 01:04:35,967
- A further warning --

1744
01:04:35,967 --> 01:04:36,929
- [Servo] Attention, camp,

1745
01:04:36,929 --> 01:04:38,574
tonight's movie is My Darling Clementine.

1746
01:04:38,574 --> 01:04:39,936
- When the governments of all

1747
01:04:39,936 --> 01:04:43,233
the nations do not accept my terms --

1748
01:04:43,233 --> 01:04:44,528
- I will be very put out.

1749
01:04:44,528 --> 01:04:48,695
- In four day's time, I will
bring desolation to mankind.

1750
01:04:51,298 --> 01:04:52,131
- [Servo] But first, a message

1751
01:04:52,131 --> 01:04:55,543
for True Value hardware stores.

1752
01:04:55,543 --> 01:04:58,080
- Meanwhile, Euell Gibbons
hears the call of nature.

1753
01:04:58,080 --> 01:04:58,913
(whistles)

1754
01:04:58,913 --> 01:05:00,697
(speaks in foreign language)

1755
01:05:00,697 --> 01:05:02,947
- [Joel] Incoming sentence!

1756
01:05:06,719 --> 01:05:08,548
(sighs)

1757
01:05:08,548 --> 01:05:10,697
- That's easy for you to say.

1758
01:05:10,697 --> 01:05:11,846
- [Servo] You know, maybe
there's some deep meaning

1759
01:05:11,846 --> 01:05:15,170
to this movie, that
we're just not getting.

1760
01:05:15,170 --> 01:05:16,253
Or maybe not.

1761
01:05:18,415 --> 01:05:20,404
- He's dying of Legionnaire's disease.

1762
01:05:20,404 --> 01:05:21,472
- [Servo] Shriners.
- [Joel] Shriners.

1763
01:05:21,472 --> 01:05:23,368
- Oh, oh, yeah.

1764
01:05:23,368 --> 01:05:24,209
- [Servo] Don't you wish?

1765
01:05:24,209 --> 01:05:26,292
(laughs)

1766
01:05:28,415 --> 01:05:29,248
- Typical Shriner.

1767
01:05:29,248 --> 01:05:31,820
Smashed his midget Mustang into a pole.

1768
01:05:31,820 --> 01:05:33,987
- [Servo] Yep, sad really.

1769
01:05:35,344 --> 01:05:38,575
Well, now this con's
sneakin' into a petting zoo.

1770
01:05:38,575 --> 01:05:39,408
- Heavy.

1771
01:05:42,140 --> 01:05:45,807
- [Joel] Alexander
Monday, It Takes A Thief.

1772
01:05:47,321 --> 01:05:49,730
- I'll take those boots, Mr. Bond.

1773
01:05:49,730 --> 01:05:52,416
(thud)

1774
01:05:52,416 --> 01:05:53,751
- [Servo] How the devil did I do that?

1775
01:05:53,751 --> 01:05:57,623
I couldn't do that again, if I tried.

1776
01:05:57,623 --> 01:05:59,719
- [Omar] Did you get close to the castle?

1777
01:05:59,719 --> 01:06:01,161
- [Servo] Close to Picasso?

1778
01:06:01,161 --> 01:06:02,328
- Yes, master.

1779
01:06:03,337 --> 01:06:06,077
- Jelly donut got away from you, huh?

1780
01:06:06,077 --> 01:06:07,078
- [Omar] Speak.

1781
01:06:07,078 --> 01:06:07,911
(dog barking)

1782
01:06:07,911 --> 01:06:11,161
- There are 50 men guarding the castle.

1783
01:06:12,032 --> 01:06:12,873
- [Joel] Oh, great.

1784
01:06:12,873 --> 01:06:15,383
He's the only one who knows
the plot, and he's dying.

1785
01:06:15,383 --> 01:06:16,883
- [Servo] Typical.

1786
01:06:17,791 --> 01:06:20,208
- Their leader still lives...

1787
01:06:22,833 --> 01:06:25,166
Says Fu Manchu's a prisoner.

1788
01:06:30,123 --> 01:06:31,258
- It was Callahan!

1789
01:06:31,258 --> 01:06:32,091
Callahan did it!

1790
01:06:32,091 --> 01:06:32,954
I have my rights.

1791
01:06:32,954 --> 01:06:34,729
I have my rights!

1792
01:06:34,729 --> 01:06:36,979
