2179
01:22:08,273 --> 01:22:10,174
I'm bald, bite me, what does that mean?

2180
01:22:10,174 --> 01:22:12,844
Wait a minute, after him!

2181
01:22:12,844 --> 01:22:14,011
- The formula.

2182
01:22:16,240 --> 01:22:20,323
With this, I can control
all things, and all men.

2183
01:22:21,262 --> 01:22:23,357
- [Joel] But women, hey,
who can control women?

2184
01:22:23,357 --> 01:22:24,910
Are you with me on this, guys, huh?

2185
01:22:24,910 --> 01:22:26,390
- Flash the signal.

2186
01:22:26,390 --> 01:22:28,422
- [Servo] Not the Fisher flash.

2187
01:22:28,422 --> 01:22:31,339
(upbeat pop music)

2188
01:22:35,663 --> 01:22:36,708
- [Joel] Hey, it's Spalding Gray,

2189
01:22:36,708 --> 01:22:39,248
he's having his perfect moment.

2190
01:22:39,248 --> 01:22:41,077
- [Crow] Spalding, man.

2191
01:22:41,077 --> 01:22:42,660
You're out too far.

2192
01:22:44,603 --> 01:22:45,924
This is supposed to be like a triathlon.

2193
01:22:45,924 --> 01:22:49,697
You swim, job, then
appear in a boring movie.

2194
01:22:49,697 --> 01:22:50,655
- [Joel] Yeah, well, I'll have

2195
01:22:50,655 --> 01:22:53,093
you know that Roger Ebert liked this film.

2196
01:22:53,093 --> 01:22:54,013
- I'll have you know, the only thing

2197
01:22:54,013 --> 01:22:56,794
Roger Ebert likes is big pans of lasagna.

2198
01:22:56,794 --> 01:22:59,377
- [Servo] Lots of them.

2199
01:22:59,377 --> 01:23:00,320
Chafe, ooh, chafe ooh.

2200
01:23:00,320 --> 01:23:01,365
Ooh, chafe.

2201
01:23:01,365 --> 01:23:02,483
Oh, these corduroys.

2202
01:23:02,483 --> 01:23:03,614
Oh, chafe, chafe.

2203
01:23:03,614 --> 01:23:05,781
Ooh, ooh, ooh, chafe, ooh.

2204
01:23:08,520 --> 01:23:10,551
(humming)

2205
01:23:10,551 --> 01:23:11,509
(kiss smacks)

2206
01:23:11,509 --> 01:23:12,342
- [Kessler] Bad dreams?

2207
01:23:12,342 --> 01:23:14,252
- [Crow] You just kissed
the back of my head.

2208
01:23:14,252 --> 01:23:16,864
- [Ingrid] The worst dreams
are better than reality.

2209
01:23:16,864 --> 01:23:18,983
- [Kessler] Why?

2210
01:23:18,983 --> 01:23:23,020
Think that maybe, without
this awful adventure,

2211
01:23:23,020 --> 01:23:27,171
we would never have realized
that we were in love.

2212
01:23:27,171 --> 01:23:28,303
- [Crow] Now that we're going to die,

2213
01:23:28,303 --> 01:23:31,426
I could tell you a
thousand, wonderful hours.

2214
01:23:31,426 --> 01:23:32,645
- [Kessler] I didn't see.

2215
01:23:32,645 --> 01:23:34,822
- [Ingrid] I didn't want you to see it.

2216
01:23:34,822 --> 01:23:35,683
- [Joel] Nobody can see.

2217
01:23:35,683 --> 01:23:37,265
- [Ingrid] I didn't want to
distract you from your work,

2218
01:23:37,265 --> 01:23:40,648
your experiments, your investigations,

2219
01:23:40,648 --> 01:23:44,344
which were all so much
more important than me.

2220
01:23:44,344 --> 01:23:45,177
(kiss smack)

2221
01:23:45,177 --> 01:23:46,239
- [Servo] You just kissed
me, full on the eyeball.

2222
01:23:46,239 --> 01:23:49,432
- [Kessler] You're exactly right, Ingrid.

2223
01:23:49,432 --> 01:23:50,724
(spitting)

2224
01:23:50,724 --> 01:23:53,057
- I've got hair in my mouth.

2225
01:23:54,236 --> 01:23:55,069
- [Servo] Bump!

2226
01:23:55,069 --> 01:23:55,902
Ooh, my toe.

2227
01:23:55,902 --> 01:23:56,735
Boom!

2228
01:23:56,735 --> 01:23:57,735
Oh, my face.

2229
01:24:02,653 --> 01:24:05,106
- [Kessler] Thanks to those
many hours of hard work,

2230
01:24:05,106 --> 01:24:08,139
during the Professor's operation,
I managed to gain access

2231
01:24:08,139 --> 01:24:12,306
to some acid, which I can
now use against Fu Manchu.

2232
01:24:14,461 --> 01:24:16,338
- [Servo] Why didn't you do this earlier?

2233
01:24:16,338 --> 01:24:18,065
- [Crow] He wanted to
make time with a woman.

2234
01:24:18,065 --> 01:24:19,148
- [Servo] Oh.

2235
01:24:21,389 --> 01:24:22,222
(explosion)

2236
01:24:22,222 --> 01:24:25,222
- [Joel] Tony Blake is The Magician.

2237
01:24:29,530 --> 01:24:30,488
Oh, the acid!

2238
01:24:30,488 --> 01:24:31,988
Ow, it's stinging.

2239
01:24:33,811 --> 01:24:35,887
(suspenseful music)

2240
01:24:35,887 --> 01:24:39,283
- [Servo] It looks like
the opening of Mod Squad.

2241
01:24:39,283 --> 01:24:40,574
(yells)

2242
01:24:40,574 --> 01:24:41,407
Oops!

2243
01:24:41,407 --> 01:24:42,240
- [Nayland] Keep quiet!

2244
01:24:42,240 --> 01:24:43,073
I shan't hurt you.

2245
01:24:43,073 --> 01:24:43,906
I'm from the --

2246
01:24:43,906 --> 01:24:44,742
- [Servo] I shall.

2247
01:24:44,742 --> 01:24:47,108
- Fu Manchu intends to destroy Istanbul!

2248
01:24:47,108 --> 01:24:47,941
- [Servo] What?

2249
01:24:47,941 --> 01:24:48,774
- Please!

2250
01:24:48,774 --> 01:24:49,981
- [Nayland] Is there a radio transmitter?

2251
01:24:49,981 --> 01:24:51,098
- Yes, I can guide you.

2252
01:24:51,098 --> 01:24:51,931
Follow me!

2253
01:24:53,217 --> 01:24:54,050
- [Lin Tang] Father!

2254
01:24:54,050 --> 01:24:56,497
- Are they celebrating Hanukkah?

2255
01:24:56,497 --> 01:24:57,905
- [Lin Tang] Father!

2256
01:24:57,905 --> 01:25:00,256
Dr. Kessler and the
girl, they have escaped.

2257
01:25:00,256 --> 01:25:02,673
They have reached the tunnel.

2258
01:25:03,558 --> 01:25:04,391
(grunts)

2259
01:25:04,391 --> 01:25:07,175
- [Joel] I've been sitting too long.

2260
01:25:07,175 --> 01:25:09,090
You know, he looks like Bill Wyman.

2261
01:25:09,090 --> 01:25:10,507
- [Crow] He does.

2262
01:25:12,689 --> 01:25:14,300
- They will die.

2263
01:25:14,300 --> 01:25:16,071
- [Servo] Neat.

2264
01:25:16,071 --> 01:25:17,159
- How is Booth?

2265
01:25:17,159 --> 01:25:18,146
- [Joel] No.
- [Crow] No?

2266
01:25:18,146 --> 01:25:20,485
- [Joel] No.
- [Crow] Oh.

2267
01:25:20,485 --> 01:25:24,568
- [Servo] Not with that
Etch A Sketch, you won't.

2268
01:25:25,637 --> 01:25:26,479
- We're through!

2269
01:25:26,479 --> 01:25:27,597
- [Servo] I don't love you anymore.

2270
01:25:27,597 --> 01:25:28,728
- This is Nayland Smith,

2271
01:25:28,728 --> 01:25:32,023
speaking from Fu Manchu's headquarters.

2272
01:25:32,023 --> 01:25:34,005
Send a warning to the Bosphorus!

2273
01:25:34,005 --> 01:25:34,969
- [Servo] Yeah, right.

2274
01:25:34,969 --> 01:25:38,321
Come on Mickey Mouse,
broadcasting from Disneyland.

2275
01:25:38,321 --> 01:25:40,164
- Nayland Smith.

2276
01:25:40,164 --> 01:25:40,997
(explosion)

2277
01:25:40,997 --> 01:25:41,830
Come on!

2278
01:25:41,830 --> 01:25:42,663
- [Joel] Whoa, getting a little feedback.

2279
01:25:42,663 --> 01:25:45,334
Those old tube amps are quirky.

2280
01:25:45,334 --> 01:25:48,625
(suspenseful music)

2281
01:25:48,625 --> 01:25:49,458
- [Servo] Well, she
gained a little weight.

2282
01:25:49,458 --> 01:25:50,791
- [Joel] Mm-hmm.

2283
01:25:54,778 --> 01:25:58,348
- Uh-oh, it's after five, the
gateway to eternity's closed!

2284
01:25:58,348 --> 01:26:01,265
Yes, yes, dear, I'm doing it, dear.

2285
01:26:05,213 --> 01:26:06,374
- Look!

2286
01:26:06,374 --> 01:26:08,040
- [Joel] You're wonderful,
I could kiss you.

2287
01:26:08,040 --> 01:26:11,015
- [Nayland] This way, through the door!

2288
01:26:11,015 --> 01:26:13,635
- [Servo] Remember to keep
left through eternity.

2289
01:26:13,635 --> 01:26:17,135
- [Crow] Not that way, that's immortality!

2290
01:26:18,424 --> 01:26:19,382
(sniffs)

2291
01:26:19,382 --> 01:26:21,399
- [Servo] It's lemon-y Rosco fog.

2292
01:26:21,399 --> 01:26:23,066
- I love that stuff.

2293
01:26:24,171 --> 01:26:25,004
(sniffs)

2294
